hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9601","And with his isnad he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel of death used to come to people visibly, then he came to Musa son of Imran (peace be upon him) and he struck him and poked out his eye, and the angel of death ascended and said: O Lord, Your servant Musa did such and such to me, and were it not for his honor with You, I would have been severe with him. Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Go to Musa My servant and give him the choice between placing his hand on the back of a bull, so for every hair his palm covers he gets a year, or dying now. So he came to him and gave him the choice. Musa said: What is after that? He said: Death. He said: Then now. He said: So he took his soul, and Allah, blessed and exalted, restored his sight - meaning upon the angel of death - and after that he came to people secretly. And this hadith has been narrated on the story of Musa from other than the hadith of Ammar: Ibn Tawus narrated it from his father from Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know anyone attributed this hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Abu Hurayrah."
"9602","Abu Rafi: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah and Matar, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he sits between her four parts and then exerts himself, ghusl has become obligatory. And in the hadith of Matar: Even if he does not ejaculate."
"9603","And Abdulquddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abdilkarim narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah and Matar, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9604","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had one of them known, when he attends the prayer, that he would get a limb of a fat sheep, he would have done it, and what he gets of reward is greater than that. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9605","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The deaf one who hears nothing, the fool, the senile, and a man who died in the fatrah will be presented before Allah. The deaf one will say: O Lord, Islam came and I heard nothing. The fool will say: O Lord, Islam came and I understood nothing. The one who died in the fatrah will say: O Lord, no messenger of Yours came to me. - Abu Bakr al-Bazzar said: And what the fourth said escaped me - He said: So He will take their covenants that they will obey Him, then He, blessed and exalted, will send to them: Enter the Fire. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, had they entered it, it would have been coolness and safety upon them."
"9606","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, with the like of this hadith, except that he said at its end: Whoever entered it, it was coolness and safety upon him, and whoever did not enter it entered the Fire. And these words have been narrated from other than Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad, and it has been narrated from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from al-Aswad ibn Sari from more than one angle, and from Anas ibn Malik, and from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"9607","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Said al-Haddad Ahmad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Surur ibn al-Mughirah al-Wasiti Abu Amir narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had the Children of Israel taken the lowest cow, it would have sufficed them. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad."
"9608","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Qasim Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade fasting on Friday. And these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from more than one angle: al-Amash narrated it from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, and Abdilmalik ibn Umayr narrated it from Abul Awbar from Abu Hurayrah, and narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr, and from Juwayriyah, and from Junadah al-Azdi."
"9609","Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that two men brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and neither of them had proof, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to draw lots over the oath, whether they liked it or disliked it."
"9610","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Said al-Attar narrated to us, they said: Abu Qatan Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had you known - or: had they known - Abu Qatan doubted - what is in the first row, there would have been nothing but drawing lots. And this hadith: similar to it was narrated by Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, and Abu az-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah with other than its wording, and the hadith of Shubah: we do not know anyone narrated it from Shubah except Abu Qatan."
"9611","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abdurrahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Zakariyya (peace be upon him) was a carpenter. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9612","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: There was a black woman who swept the mosque, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed her and asked about her, and they said: She died. So he came to her grave and prayed over her. And this hadith was narrated by Hammad ibn Zayd from Thabit from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah, and Habib ibn ash-Shahid and Abu Amir al-Kharraz narrated it from Thabit from Anas, and al-Ala ibn Abdirrahman narrated it from his father from Abu Hurayrah, and it was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from several angles: Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah narrated it from his father, and ash-Shabi and Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated it from Ibn Abbas, and narrated from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from his father, and from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, and from Abu Umamah Abdullah ibn Thalabah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9613","Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn ash-Shikhir: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Farqad narrated to us in the house of Qatadah, from Abu al-Ala, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most lying of people are the dyers and the goldsmiths. And we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9614","Al-Ajjaj Abu Ru'bah: Rufay ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muammar ibn al-Muthanna Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Ru'bah ibn al-Ajjaj, from his father, that he asked Abu Hurayrah and said: O Abu Hurayrah, what do you say about this: With a cleft chin? Abu Hurayrah said: We used to recite this in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not fault it. And we do not know that Ru'bah ibn al-Ajjaj nor his father transmitted except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it except Abu Hurayrah."
"9615","Amr ibn Maymun: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise beneath the Throne? And that you say: There is no power except with Allah. Allah says: My servant has submitted and surrendered."
"9616","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure of the treasure of Paradise beneath the Throne? There is no power except with Allah."
"9617","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever loves to find the taste of faith, let him love a person loving him only for Allah."
"9618","Talq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi ash-Shatha, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know anyone narrated it from Shubah from Ashath ibn Abi ash-Shatha with this isnad except Yazid ibn Harun, and he was not followed on it, and the correct in my view is the hadith of Abu Balj from Amr ibn Maymun from Abu Hurayrah."
"9619","Ash-Shabi: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Isa narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt and over her maternal aunt."
"9620","And Muhammad ibn Abdilmalik and Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, they said: Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not to be married over her paternal aunt, nor the paternal aunt over her brother's daughter, nor a woman over her maternal aunt, nor the maternal aunt over her sister's daughter, nor the elder over the younger, nor the younger over the elder. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from many angles, and there is disagreement on it from ash-Shabi: Abu Dawud said: From ash-Shabi from Abu Hurayrah. Asim al-Ahwal said: From ash-Shabi from Jabir. Jabir al-Jufi said: From ash-Shabi from Abu Said al-Khudri."
"9621","Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us with it, Yazid ibn Zuray and al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"9622","Muhammad ibn Abdilmalik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried or its matter is concluded has two qirats."
"9623","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Adam and Musa argued with each other. Musa said: You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit; you took us out of Paradise. He said: And you are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and with His speech; do you find that written upon me before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: So Adam overcame Musa."
"9624","Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn ar-Rawwas narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Three things I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Banu Tamim; I will never hate Banu Tamim after them: Aishah had a freed slave from the offspring of Ismail to free as a vow, then captives from Banu al-Anbar were taken, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, if it pleases you to fulfill your vow, free a freed one from these. So he made them from the offspring of Ismail. And charity camels of Banu Sad were brought, and when he saw them coming in the evening, he said: These are the camels of my people. So he made them his people. And he said: They are the fiercest of people in fighting in the great battles. And we do not know this hadith narrated from ash-Shabi except Dawud, and Abdilwarith narrated it from Dawud, and it is Maslamah through whom he is known, and Abdulwarith narrated it, and it is more famous with Maslamah."
"9625","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Umar ibn Habib narrated to us, from Dawud, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour; no servant meets it asking Allah for good in it except He gives it to him."
"9626","And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from more than one angle, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Dawud except Umar ibn Habib and Maslamah, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Maslamah except Ubaydullah ibn Umar, and al-Fadl narrated it to us from Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Maslamah, and Umar ibn Habib was a well-known man but was not a memorizer."
"9627","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nayzak al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sayyar, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of pebbles. And this hadith is not known narrated from Shubah except Rawh, and few narrated it from Rawh: Ahmad ibn Hanbal and more than one narrated it."
"9628","And Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the high ranks will be seen by those below them as the brilliant star is seen on the horizon of the sky, and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from ash-Shabi from Abu Hurayrah except Abu Qutaybah."
"9629","And Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A riding animal held as pledge may be ridden for its upkeep when it is pawned, and the milk of a milch animal may be drunk when it is pawned, and upon the one who drinks and rides is its upkeep. And we do not know this hadith narrated from ash-Shabi except Zakariyya, and al-Amash narrated it from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that he said: The pledge is ridden and milked, but he did not explain it."
"9630","Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the earth will split, then I will raise my head and find Musa son of Imran; I do not know whether he is among those whom Allah exempted or he raised his head before me."
"9631","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abdilhamid narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from ash-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed dates among his companions, and some of them would join two together, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining two except with the permission of one's companion. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ata ibn as-Saib from ash-Shabi from Abu Hurayrah except Jarir, and Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Ata ibn as-Saib from Ajlan from Abu Hurayrah."
"9632","Said ibn Jubayr: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abdirrahim ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Shabib, from Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were there in the mosque a hundred thousand or more, then a man of the people of the Fire breathed, he would burn them. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know for it a path other than this path, and this hadith was narrated from Hisham by Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad and Abdirrahim, and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Musa from Abdirrahim, and this hadith is known only through Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad Abdulwahid ibn Wasil."
"9633","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Habib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: not to sleep except upon witr, fasting three days of every month, and ghusl on Friday - or: the two rakahs of Duha - Abu Bakr doubts. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Said ibn Jubayr from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle, though it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through many paths."
"9634","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shabib, from Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, that he would hear the muadh-dhin calling the adhan and say: I bear witness to it with every witness and I undertake it on behalf of every denier."
"9635","Al-Aswad ibn Hilal: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to sleep upon witr, ghusl on Friday, and fasting three days of every month. Ahmad said: And we do not know that al-Aswad ibn Hilal narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9636","Salim ibn Abi al-Jad: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man nor for one possessing sound strength. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah from Mansur from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, and the correct is the hadith of Israil from Mansur from Salim from Abu Hurayrah, and Israil was followed in his narration by Abu Husayn, who narrated it from Salim from Abu Hurayrah."
"9637","Ibrahim ibn al-Mujashshir al-Baghdadi narrated it to us with it, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man nor for one possessing sound strength."
"9638","Yazid ibn Sharik: Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, from Yazid ibn Sharik, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will soon wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades and that he had never taken charge of any affair of people."
"9639","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The destruction of the Arabs is at the hands of young lads - or he said: lads - of Quraysh. Marwan said: Evil lads are those. And we do not know that Yazid ibn Sharik narrated from Abu Hurayrah except these two hadiths."
"9640","Ziyad ibn Qays: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban - meaning Ibn Abdirrahman an-Nahwi - from Asim, from Ziyad ibn Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the Arabs from an approaching evil. And these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from several angles, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ziyad ibn Qays except Asim, nor did Ziyad ibn Qays narrate from Abu Hurayrah except two hadiths, this being one of them, and the other:"
"9641","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Asim, from Ziyad ibn Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say: There is no god but Allah, their blood and wealth become inviolable except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah. And these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from more than one angle, and narrated from other than Abu Hurayrah."
"9642","Abu al-Ahwas: Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Abi ash-Shatha, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-five degrees. And these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from several angles, and we do not know for it a path from Abu al-Ahwas except this path, and Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Abu Hurayrah two hadiths with this isnad, this being one of them, and the other:"
"9643","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us with it, Abu an-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah Shayban, meaning Ibn Abdirrahman, narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi ash-Shatha, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour; He does not ask Allah for anything in it except He gives it to him - meaning His servant. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ashath except Shayban."
"9644","Kumayl ibn Ziyad: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdirrahman ibn Abis, from Kumayl ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except with Allah. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Shubah except Harami ibn Umarah and Kumayl ibn Ziyad, and Abdirrahman ibn Abis and Abu Ishaq narrated from him. As for what Abu Ishaq narrated from Kumayl ibn Ziyad an-Nakhai from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of the walled gardens of Madinah, and he said to me: O Abu Hurayrah. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The much-wealthy are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection except one who says thus with his wealth and thus, motioning with his hand to his right and to his left, and few are they. Then he said: O Abu Hurayrah, shall I not guide you to a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: There is no power nor strength except with Allah; there is no refuge nor escape from Allah except to Him. Then he said: O Abu Hurayrah, do you know what is Allah's right upon servants and what is the servants' right upon Allah? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Allah's right upon servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and a right upon Allah is that He not punish one who associates nothing with Him."
"9645","Muhammad ibn Muammar narrated to us with this hadith, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Kumayl ibn Ziyad an-Nakhai, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9646","Kulayb Abu Asim ibn Kulayb: Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh and Muhammad ibn Muammar narrated to us, they said: Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed Duha only once. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Asim except Sufyan, and Waki and Qabisah narrated it from Sufyan."
"9647","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Salih ibn Mihran narrated to us, an-Numan ibn Abdissalam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray until his feet swelled, and he was spoken to about that, so he said: Shall I not be a grateful servant?"
"9648","And Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And I do not know this hadith narrated from Sufyan except an-Numan ibn Abdissalam, nor from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Yahya ibn Fudayl."
"9649","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every sermon in which there is no testimony is like a leprous hand. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Asim ibn Kulayb except Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad."
"9650","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The truthful and believed Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, he said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from several angles."
"9651","Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard from Abul Qasim, the truthful and believed, saying: The one-eyed Dajjal, the messiah of misguidance, will come out toward the east, in a time of disagreement and division among people, and will reach what Allah wills him to reach of the earth in forty days - Allah knows best what its measure is - and the believers will meet severe hardship. Then Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon him) will descend from heaven and lead people in prayer; when he raises his head from his bowing, he will say: Allah hears whoever praises Him; Allah has killed the Dajjal and the believers have prevailed. So I swear that the Messenger of Allah, Abul Qasim, the truthful and believed (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: It is true and near, for all that is coming is near."
"9652","And Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This fire of yours and every fire kindled - or: they kindle - is a part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell."
"9653","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the best charity is what leaves sufficiency, and begin with those you support."
"9654","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"9655","Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever's molar tooth is like Uhud, his thigh like al-Warqan, and the thickness of his skin forty cubits. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah with a better isnad than this isnad, and we heard it only from al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad al-Kufi."
"9656","Yazid ibn al-Awdi: Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father and his uncle Dawud, from their father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What I fear most for you are the two hollows: the mouth and the private part. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Idris except his son, and more than one narrated it from Dawud."
"9657","Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dream is a part of forty-six, or forty-seven, parts of prophethood. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Idris except his son."
"9658","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi and al-Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us, they said: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Idris ibn Yazid narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two rivers of Paradise: the Nile and the Euphrates. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Idris except Marwan and Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Ansari."
"9659","Ibrahim ibn Malik narrated it to us with it, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Idris, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9660","And Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Aswad ibn Salim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will never encompass people with your wealth, but what encompasses them from you is a cheerful face and good character. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Idris from his father from his grandfather from Abu Hurayrah except Aswad ibn Salim, and he was a trustworthy Baghdadi."
"9661","Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Abu as-Sari Sahl ibn Mahmud narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of people to perish are the Persians, and after them the Arabs. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Idris from his father from his grandfather from Abu Hurayrah except Sahl ibn Mahmud, and he was a trustworthy Baghdadi, and this hadith is known only from the hadith of Dawud al-Awdi."
"9662","Bundar narrated to us, Said ibn ar-Rabi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Idris, he said: I heard my father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I think, and my greatest knowledge is that it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you should pray while there is any impurity on him, or while he is holding back impurity. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"9663","Ahmad ibn Yahya as-Sufi narrated to us, a man he named - his name escaped me at this time - narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Dawud and Idris, from their father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9664","And I found in my book, from Muhammad ibn Miskin, from Abdullah ibn Yusuf, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Idris, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Of whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Idris from his father from Abu Hurayrah except Mansur and Ikrimah, and it is known only from the hadith of Dawud al-Awdi, and Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad combined them both."
"9665","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of swearing oaths, for it sells the goods but erases - I think he said: blessing. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Idris except Hafs, nor from Hafs except Sahl."
"9666","Muhammad ibn Muammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Dawud ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The praised station is intercession. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"9667","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what admits people into Paradise? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Fear of Allah and good character. Do you know what most admits people into the Fire? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The two hollows: the mouth and the private part."
"9668","Ali ibn Shubrumah al-Bahili narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to him and said: I adjure you by Allah, if I ask you about a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrate it to me. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Of whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him? He said: O Allah, yes."
"9669","Sahl ibn Bahr al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated to us, as-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in the woman, the house, and the horse. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle, nor did anyone narrate it from Dawud except as-Sabbah ibn Muharib."
"9670","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Kufi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Dawud ibn Yazid narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the fourth, forever until the Hour is established. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle."
"9671","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Dawud ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Sad came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the face of Sad there is good. He said: O Messenger of Allah, Kisra has perished. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of people to perish are the Persians and the Arabs."
"9672","Abu Khalid al-Walibi: Hisham ibn Yunus al-Kufi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Imran ibn Zaidah ibn Nashit narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night, would lower his voice at times and raise it at times. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad, and more than one narrated it from Imran."
"9673","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Imran ibn Zaidah ibn Nashit narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: O son of Adam, free your heart for Me; I will fill your heart with richness and close your poverty, and if you do not free your heart for Me, I will fill your heart with poverty and not close your need. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad."
"9674","Abu ash-Shatha al-Muharibi: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi ash-Shatha, from his father, who said: We were with Abu Hurayrah in the mosque when the muadh-dhin called the adhan and a man left the mosque. Abu Hurayrah said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9675","Amr ibn Asim: Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yala ibn Ata narrated to us, from Amr ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, command me something to say when I wake in the morning and when I enter the evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of all things and their Owner, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and the evil of Satan and his associating; say it when you wake in the morning, when you enter the evening, and when you take your bed."
"9676","And Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know that Amr ibn Asim narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9677","Malik ibn Zalimm: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Malik ibn Zalimm, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The destruction of my nation is at the hands of young lads of Quraysh."
"9678","And Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated it to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zaidah ibn Qudamah, from Simak, from Malik ibn Zalimm, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know that Malik ibn Zalimm narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9679","Al-Walid ibn Abdirrahman: Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from al-Walid ibn Abdirrahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits until it is buried has two qirats. Ibn Umar denied that, so they sent to Aishah and asked her, and she said: He spoke the truth - meaning Abu Hurayrah."
"9680","Ziyad ibn Makhzum: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ziyad, the freedman of Banu Makhzum, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection."
"9681","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Kisra after Kisra, nor Qaysar after Qaysar, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the path of Allah."
"9682","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will enter Paradise by his deed. They said: Not even you? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"9683","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ziyad, and he did not attribute him, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guest has three days upon the one with whom he stays; what is beyond that is charity, and upon the guest is to depart, not burdening the people of the house with sin."
"9684","Abu Zibyan: I heard Amr ibn Ali saying: I heard al-Hasan ibn as-Sakan narrating from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Everything has a choicest part, and the choicest part of prayer is the first takbir. Amr ibn Ali mentioned it in disapproval of al-Hasan ibn as-Sakan, and I memorized it from him and wrote it without him dictating it to Amr ibn Ali, and he was not pleased with this shaykh."
"9685","Abu Alqamah: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9686","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to seek refuge from five: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal."
"9687","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When Kisra perishes there is no Kisra, and when Qaysar perishes there is no Qaysar after him."
"9688","Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Yahya at-Taymi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9689","And Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9690","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abdilhamid narrated to us, from Layth, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No servant seeks refuge from the Fire seven times except the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from me, and none asks Paradise seven times except Paradise says: O Allah, settle him in me - or a word like it."
"9691","Ibrahim ibn Nasr ar-Razi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yala ibn Ata informed us, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me; the commander is a shield: when he says takbir, say takbir, when he bows, bow, when he prostrates, prostrate; if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise; and when he recites: Nor of those astray, say: Amin; when the people of heaven agree with the saying of the people of earth, the servant is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"9692","Abu Razin: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises at night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9693","And Amr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9694","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abdirrahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abdulwahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, Abu Salih and Abu Razin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times, and when the strap of one's sandal breaks, let him not walk in one sandal."
"9695","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Taghlib narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"9696","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of one's sandal breaks, let him not walk in one sandal until he repairs his strap."
"9697","Abdullah ibn Ziyad ar-Razi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman ar-Razi narrated to us, Abu Sinan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am a blind man, my house is far, and I have a guide who does not suit me; do you find for me any concession? He said: Do you hear the call? He said: Yes. He said: I find no excuse for you - or he said: concession. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Amr ibn Murrah from Abu Razin from Abu Hurayrah except Abu Sinan."
"9698","Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Bayan ibn Humran narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, the brother of Mubarak ibn Fudalah, narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sponsors an orphan, whether related to him or not, he and I will be in Paradise like these two - joining his two fingers - and whoever strives for three daughters is in Paradise, and it is for him like the reward of a warrior in the path of Allah, fasting and standing in prayer. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad, and al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah is a well-known Basran, and they are brothers: Mubarak ibn Fudalah, al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, and Ubaydurrahman ibn Fudalah."
"9699","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two Muslims lose three children and accept it patiently except they will be a wall for them between them and the Fire."
"9700","And Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Asim, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whose three children die before reaching maturity, he will enter Paradise. They said: And two? He said: And two."
"9701","Abu ar-Rabi: Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, from Abu ar-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things not to leave them: the Duha prayer, not to sleep except upon witr, and fasting three days of every month."
"9702","Amr ibn Ali and Abu Yazid Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Simak, from Abu ar-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once, and he said: Whoever spreads his garment, I will not narrate a hadith - I think he said: except he will memorize it. So I spread my garment, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated many hadiths, and I gathered my garment, and I forgot nothing of his hadith. This hadith is not known narrated from Shubah from Simak from Abu ar-Rabi from Abu Hurayrah except Ibn Abi Adi."
"9703","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, from Abu ar-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it: When the servant draws near to Allah, blessed and exalted, by a span, He draws near to him by a cubit. And we memorized this hadith only from Amr ibn Ali from Abu Dawud with this isnad."
"9704","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abu ar-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four things people will not abandon of the affairs of ignorance: reviling lineages, wailing, and their saying: We were given rain by such and such star. And I think that Umar narrated it to us also from Abdirrahman from ath-Thawri."
"9705","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abu ar-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four things people will not abandon of the affairs of ignorance: wailing, mutual reproach in lineages, their saying: We were given rain by such a star, and contagion: a camel got mangy and a hundred became mangy - so who made the first mangy? And this hadith is not known narrated from Abu ar-Rabi except Alqamah ibn Marthad."
"9706","Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdirrahman al-Kufi narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Abu ar-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is wronged with an injustice and leaves it except Allah increases him with it in honor, and give charity, for no charity decreases wealth but increases it. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Alqamah from Abu ar-Rabi from Abu Hurayrah except Hisham ibn Abdirrahman al-Kufi, and none narrated it from Hisham except Abdullah ibn Ghalib al-Abbadani, and this shaykh narrated from Hisham other hadiths from al-Amash."
"9707","Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from his father: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant of one of you brings his food, let him seat him and eat with him; if he does not do so, let him give him - meaning a morsel."
"9708","Musa ibn Talhah: Muhammad ibn Abdilmalik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abdilmalik ibn Umayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When: And warn your nearest kin was revealed, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and called: O Banu Kab ibn Luayy, save yourselves from the Fire; O Banu Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire; O Banu Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire; O Banu Abdilmuttalib, save yourselves from the Fire; O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire; I own nothing for you against Allah except that you have kinship which I will keep moist with its moisture."
"9709","And Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Akhi Waki narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abdilmalik ibn Umayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"9710","Muhammad ibn Abdilmalik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abdilmalik ibn Umayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a roasted rabbit, bringing with it its side and its condiment, and placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withheld and did not eat, and ordered his companions to eat, and the Bedouin withheld and did not eat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents you from eating? He said: I fast three days of every month. He said: If you are fasting, fast the white days. And this hadith was narrated by other than Abdilmalik ibn Umayr, but they differed on Musa ibn Talhah: some narrated it from Musa ibn Talhah from Ibn al-Hawtakiyah from Abu Dharr, and some narrated it from Musa ibn Talhah from Ibn al-Hawtakiyah from Umar."
"9711","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bazi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, he said: I heard Abu Yahya, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the muadh-dhin: He is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry that hears him answers him, and the one who attends the prayer has twenty-five good deeds written for him."
"9712","Abu Kibash: Muhammad ibn Firas narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Kidam ibn Abdirrahman, from Abu Kibash, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What an excellent sacrifice is the young sheep of sheep."
"9713","Qays ibn Abi Hazim: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: We came to Abu Hurayrah to greet him, and we said: Narrate to us. He said: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three years; I was never in years more intelligent than in them, nor more loving to retain what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says. I saw him motioning with his hand: Soon, before the Hour, you will fight a people whose sandals are of hair, and you will fight a people red-faced, small-eyed, as if they are hammered shields. By Allah, for one of you to go out in the morning and gather firewood on his back and sell it and support himself with it and give charity from it is better for him than coming to a man asking him, whether he gives him or withholds from him, and that is because the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. And the breath of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9714","And Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"9715","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a trustee: if he prays standing, pray standing, if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and when he says takbir, say takbir. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from several angles, and we mentioned it from Qays from Abu Hurayrah."
"9716","Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah after Hunayn - I think he said: by three (days/nights) - and the night I intended to enter Madinah, a slave boy of mine strayed from me, and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O night of its length and its toil, yet that he saved me from the land of disbelief. While I was speaking to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), suddenly there was my slave boy. And we do not know of any chain for this hadith from Abu Hurayrah except this chain."
"9717","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nizak narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The destruction of my Ummah will be at the hands of youngsters from Quraysh. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the hadith of Ismail from Qays from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain, and similar wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other chains."
"9718","Amir ibn Sa'd al-Bajali: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Amir, from Amir ibn Sa'd al-Bajali, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A funeral bier was brought past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was praised with good, so he said: It has become due. And a funeral bier was brought past him and it was praised with evil, so he said: It has become due. Then he said: Some of you are witnesses over others."
"9719","Abu Mi'qal, a shaykh from the people of Kufa: Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abu Daws narrated to us, who said: A man called Abu Mi'qal came to me and said to me: Write. So I wrote: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me to fast three days of every month, and to sleep upon witr, and (to pray) the tasbih of al-Duha. And we do not know that this Abu Mi'qal narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9720","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Awbar - and his name is Ziyad ibn al-Harith - from Abu Hurayrah, that a man asked him and said: Did you forbid the people from fasting on Friday? He said: No, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, I did not forbid, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Friday, except that one fasts a day before it or a day after it."
"9721","Abu Hurayrah said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in his sandals."
"9722","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us this hadith, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a man from Banu al-Harith, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"9723","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Awbar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording, and he added in it: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day the morning prayer, then said: This is the wolf, and what is the wolf! He has come to you asking you to give him or to share with him in your wealth. So a man threw a stone at him, and he passed on or turned away howling. And this addition which Jarir added, we do not know anyone who narrated it other than him."
"9724","Abu Yahya, freedman of Ja'dah: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Yahya, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed so-and-so woman fasts the day and stands (in prayer) the night and harms her neighbours. So he said: There is no good in her, she is among the people of the Fire. And it was said: So-and-so woman prays the obligatory prayer and does not harm her neighbours. He said: She is among the people of Paradise."
"9725","Al-Suddi from his father: al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The restraint of faith is treacherous killing; a believer does not kill treacherously. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain."
"9726","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the dead person hears the striking of their sandals when they turn away from him. Meaning turning their backs. And we only know this hadith from al-Thawri, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9727","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard my close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer; faith is more honourable to Allah than that. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Suddi from his father from Abu Hurayrah except Abu Isra'il."
"9728","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the saying of Allah the Exalted: {The Day We shall call every people with their leader}: He said: One of them will be called and given his book in his right hand, and his body will be extended, and his face will turn white, and a crown of glistening pearl will be placed on his head, so he will go to his companions and they will see him from afar and say: O Allah, bring us this one and bless us in this one. So he will come to them and say to them: Rejoice, for indeed for every man among you is the like of this. And as for the disbeliever, his face will turn black, and his body will be extended, and his companions will see him and say: We seek refuge in Allah from this, or from the evil of this; O Allah, do not bring him to us. So he will come to them and they will say: O Allah, disgrace him. So he will say: May Allah keep you far away, for indeed for every man among you is the like of this. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain."
"9729","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Isa ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it (the crescent) and break fast upon seeing it, and if it is obscured from you then complete the number, and do not precede the month. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, except Isa ibn Umar."
"9730","And Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Abdillah and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, from his father, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not seen the like of the Fire whose fleer sleeps, and we have not seen the like of Paradise whose seeker sleeps. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Suddi from his father except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Abd al-Rahman."
"9731","Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, al-Suddi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. - I think he said: One of them with dust. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Suddi from his father from Abu Hurayrah except al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr."
"9732","Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samurah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, Mis'ar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two Umrahs expiate what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mis'ar and Sufyan from Mansur from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah except Amr ibn Muhammad."
"9733","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj to the House and does not commit rafath (obscene speech) nor fusuq (sin), returns as his mother bore him. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Mansur from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah."
"9734","al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah ibn al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever performs Hajj to the House and does not commit rafath nor fusuq, returns as his mother bore him."
"9735","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no boycotting (hijrah) beyond three (days). And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hazim except Mansur."
"9736","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one of sound able body. And others besides Ibn Uyaynah narrate this hadith from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Abu Hurayrah."
"9737","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pilgrim is forgiven, and the one for whom the pilgrim seeks forgiveness. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Husayn ibn Muhammad, and we only heard it from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id."
"9738","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The invitation on the first day is Sunnah, and the second is kindness, and the third is showing off and seeking repute. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle, and Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn is not strong, though a group of scholars narrated from him, and he has hadiths in which he was not followed."
"9739","Al-A'mash from Abu Hazim: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man calls his wife, let her answer him even if she is on the back of a camel saddle, for if he spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until morning. And a group narrated this hadith from al-A'mash from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah."
"9740","And with his chain from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not speak to: the lying ruler, the poor arrogant, and the old fornicator. And a group narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9741","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were gifted a trotter I would accept, and if I were invited to an arm (of a sheep) I would answer. And more than one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9742","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That he never criticized food at all; if he desired it he ate it, and if he did not desire it he left it. And more than one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9743","Ubayd ibn Asbat narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the dog and the earnings of the prostitute."
"9744","Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad Abu Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the dog, and the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of blood."
"9745","Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever performs Hajj to the House and does not commit rafath nor fusuq returns as his mother bore him. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah, and Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah is not a preserver."
"9746","Talhah ibn Musarrif from Abu Hazim: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj al-Kufi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi al-Arhabi narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: Whoever loves me, let him love them both. And we do not know that Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except this hadith."
"9747","Salim ibn Abi Hafsah: Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Salim ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: O Allah, indeed I love them both, so love them both."
"9748","Adi ibn Thabit: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, Adi ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The best of the children of Adam are five: Nuh, Ibrahim, Isa, Musa, and Muhammad; and the best of them is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and may Allah bless them all. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Adi ibn Thabit except Hamzah al-Zayyat."
"9749","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the Muslim eats in one intestine. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Adi from Abu Hazim except Shu'bah."
"9750","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves kala' (debts/dependents), then to Allah and His Messenger, and whoever leaves wealth, then to his heirs."
"9751","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade that a woman ask for the divorce of her sister."
"9752","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade interception (of caravans), and that a Muhajir sell for a Bedouin, and that a man outbid his brother, and (he forbade) tasriyah and najsh."
"9753","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Fudayl meaning Ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is Pure and accepts only what is pure, and indeed Allah the Blessed and Exalted commanded the believers with what He commanded the Messengers, so He said: {O messengers, eat of the pure things and do righteous deeds}, and He said: {O you who believe, spend of the pure things you have earned}. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Adi except Fudayl ibn Marzuq."
"9754","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah meaning al-Dulabi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to the desert becomes harsh, and whoever follows the hunt becomes heedless, and whoever follows the ruler is tempted. And Sharik narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara', while Ismail said: from al-Hasan, from Adi, from Abu Hazim, and al-Hasan is not a preserver."
"9755","Harun ibn Sa'd: Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Harun ibn Sa'd, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man to pray over him, and it was said to him: He left two or three dinars, he said: Two brands or three. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Harun ibn Sa'd, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except Sharik."
"9756","Abu Malik al-Ashja'i: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Tariq, and he is Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quickest of the Arab tribes to perish is Quraysh, and the Hour will not come until a woman passes by a sandal and says: This is the sandal of a Qurashi. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abu Malik, nor from Abu Malik except Yahya ibn Zakariyya, nor from Yahya except Abu Dawud al-Hafari."
"9757","Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Kufi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Abu Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that he performed ablution and went far in ablution to near his armpits, so I said to him, and he said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the ornament will reach of ablution the places of purification."
"9758","al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Abu Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I drive people away from my Hawd, as the camel-herder drives away from his cistern. They said: O Messenger of Allah, will you know us? He said: Yes, my Ummah will come to me bright-faced and bright-limbed from the traces of this ablution; this mark belongs to none other than you among the nations, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is farther than from Aylah to Aden - meaning his Hawd (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - its vessels are more numerous than the stars, and it is sweeter than honey and colder than snow; no servant drinks a drink from it and then thirsts as long as the heavens and the earth remain, and some of you will surely be turned away from it! So I shall say: My companions? And it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"9759","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no deception in prayer nor in greeting. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"9760","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah meaning Ibn Qudamah, from Maysarah al-Nahdi, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him treat his guest well. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is treating the guest well? He said: Three days, and what is beyond that is charity, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or be silent, and treat women kindly; for woman was created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its top; if you go to straighten it you break it, and if you leave it you do not see the crookedness in it, so treat women kindly. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hazim except Maysarah, and we do not know Maysarah narrated from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9761","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in the two rak'ahs of Fajr: {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"9762","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I sought permission from my Lord the Blessed and Exalted to seek forgiveness for my mother, and He did not permit me, and I sought His permission to visit her grave, and He permitted me. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9763","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his uncle: Say: There is no god but Allah, I shall testify for you with it on the Day of Resurrection. So he said: Were it not that the women of Quraysh would reproach me, I would have delighted your eye with it; they would say: Only fear carried him to that. So Allah the Exalted revealed: {Indeed you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills}."
"9764","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque, he said: Hand me the garment, O A'ishah. She said: Indeed I am not praying. He said: Indeed it is not in your hand, so she handed it to him."
"9765","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who among you is fasting today? So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am. He said: So who among you fed a poor person today? Abu Bakr said: I am. He said: So who among you visited a sick person today? Abu Bakr said: I am. He said: So who among you witnessed a funeral today? Abu Bakr said: I am. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These do not gather in a man in one day except he enters Paradise. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain."
"9766","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who calls his wife to his bed and she refuses to answer him, except the One in the heaven is angry with her until he is pleased with her."
"9767","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate against the polytheists? He said: I was only sent as a mercy and I was not sent as a punishment. And we do not know it to be narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah, with this chain."
"9768","And with his chain from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Indeed I married a woman from the Ansar, he said: Did you look at her? For indeed in the eyes of the Ansar there is something? He said: Yes. He said: For how much did you marry her? He said: For four awaq (ounces). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For four awaq?! As if you carve silver from the عرض of this mountain. And we do not know it to be narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah with this chain."
"9769","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we heard a thud, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what this is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is a stone, or a rock, that fell from seventy autumns (years) into the fire of Hell, and this is when it settled or reached its bottom. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9770","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man stayed late with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then returned to his family and found his children had been put to sleep, so he swore he would not eat, then he changed his mind and said to his wife: Wake the children. So he ate, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and sees something else better than it, let him expiate his oath and do it. And we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the narration of Yazid ibn Kaysan from him."
"9771","Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, I think he raised it, who said: Indeed the believer, death descends upon him, and he sees what he sees, and he wishes his soul would come out, and Allah loves meeting him, and indeed the believer, his soul is raised to heaven, and the souls of the believers come to him and ask him about their acquaintances among the people of the earth; if he says: I left so-and-so in the world, that pleases them, and if he says: Indeed so-and-so has died, they say: He was not brought to us. And indeed the believer is seated in his grave, and asked: Who is your Lord? So he says: My Lord is Allah, then it is said: Who is your Prophet? So he says: My Prophet is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is your religion? He says: My religion is Islam, so a door is opened for him in his grave, and he says, or it is said: Look at your place, then he sees the grave, as if it were but a nap. And when he is an enemy of Allah, death descends upon him, and he sees what he sees, and he never loves that his soul should come out, and Allah hates meeting him, so when he sits in his grave or is seated, it is said to him: Who is your Lord? So he says: I do not know, so it is said: You did not know, so a door of Hell is opened for him, then he is struck a blow that every creature hears except the two weighty ones, then it is said to him: Sleep as the manhush sleeps. So I said to Abu Hurayrah: What is the manhush? He said: The one whom beasts and snakes bite, then his grave tightens upon him. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Walid ibn al-Qasim."
"9772","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man took his son with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have mercy on him, O so-and-so? He said: Yes, by Allah, indeed I have mercy on him. He said: So Allah is more merciful to him than you. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah with this wording except with this chain."
"9773","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant says: There is no god but Allah, except the doors of the heavens are opened for it until it reaches the Throne, as long as major sins are avoided. And we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of Abu Hazim except from the narration of Yazid ibn Kaysan from him."
"9774","And Abdillah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prompt your dying ones with: There is no god but Allah. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9775","And Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall recite to you - or: Gather until I recite to you - a third of the Qur'an, so he recited to them {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"9776","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan. And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded whoever slept past the Fajr prayer to pray after the sun had risen."
"9777","Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abu Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah. And from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will gather - meaning on the Day of Resurrection - and they will come to Adam, and say: O our father, open Paradise for us. So he will say: Did anything expel you from Paradise except the sin of your father Adam? I am not the one for that, go to Ibrahim the close friend of his Lord. So Ibrahim will say: I am not the one for that, I was only a close friend from afar, go to the one whom Allah spoke to directly. So they will come to Musa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he will say: I am not the one for that, go to the word of Allah and His spirit, Isa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he will say: I am not the one for that, go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they will come to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he will intercede, and the Sirat will be laid, and the first of you will pass like lightning, I said: By my father and mother, then like the wind, and birds, and the running of men, and your Prophet is upon the Sirat, saying: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. Until people cross, until a man comes who cannot except crawl, and on the sides of the Sirat are suspended hooks that seize whomever they are commanded to seize, so one scratched but saved, and one heaped into the Fire. Then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, indeed the bottom of Hell is seventy autumns (deep). And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah, nor from Hudhayfah, except with this chain."
"9778","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abu Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah. And from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah caused those before us to stray from Friday, so for the Jews is Saturday and for the Christians is Sunday; we are the last in the world, the first on the Day of Resurrection, forgiven before the creatures. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah, nor from Hudhayfah, except with this chain."
"9779","Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I was among seventy of the people of al-Suffah, none of them had a cloak upon him, they only tied their waist-wrappers at their necks, some reaching half the shins, and some reaching the ankles, gesturing with his hand for fear his private part would be seen."
"9780","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth will cast out its treasures, and the thief will pass and say: For this my hand was cut, and the killer will come and say: For this I killed, and the severer of kinship will come and say: For this I severed my kinship, then they will leave it and take nothing from it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ibn Fudayl, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9781","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, with similar wording to the hadith of al-Minhal, from Zadham, from al-Bara', except that he said: He has seen certainty for the first believer, and it is said to the wicked, and he mentioned a word, and no creature remains on earth except it enters his body. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except Fudayl, from Ghazwan, nor from Fudayl except his son Muhammad."
"9782","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man to pray over him, and it was said to him: He left two or three dinars, so he said: Two brands or three."
"9783","Muhammad ibn Sudran and Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, they said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, who said: Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad rub his face in the dust among you? They said: Yes. He said: By al-Lat and al-Uzza, if I see him doing it I shall surely tread upon his neck and surely rub his face in the dust. He said: So it was said to him one day: There he is, praying. So he came, claiming he would do to him what he said, he said: And nothing startled the people except that he was retreating on his heels and shielding himself with his hands, so the people came to him and said: What is wrong with you, O Abu al-Hakam? He said: Indeed between me and him is a trench of fire, and terror and wings. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he drawn near to me, the angels would have seized him limb by limb. He said: So Allah revealed to His Prophet: {Have you seen the one who forbids * a servant when he prays * Have you seen if he is upon guidance * or enjoins piety * Have you seen if he denies and turns away * Does he not know that Allah sees * No! If he does not desist, We shall drag him by the forelock * a lying, sinning forelock * Then let him call his assembly * We shall call the Zabaniyah}, the angels said: {No! Do not obey him}. He said: And he was commanded with what he was commanded with. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, except Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, nor did anyone narrate it from Nu'aym except al-Taymi."
"9784","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three whom Allah hates: a lying king, a poor arrogant, and a rich miser. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"9785","al-Walid ibn Sufyan al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not linger (in obscenity) nor commit fusuq, returns as his mother bore him."
"9786","Abu Zur'ah from Abu Hurayrah: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks people for their wealth, it is as if he asks for embers, so let him take little of it or much."
"9787","And Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave, he said on the third: And those who shorten."
"9788","Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Who is more unjust than one who creates like My creation, so let him create a mosquito."
"9789","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave glad tidings to Khadijah of a house of hollow pearls."
"9790","And Muhammad ibn Yazid and Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its west, and when it rises - I think he said: - no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"9791","And Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two words light upon the tongue, heavy in the scale, beloved to the Most Merciful: Glory be to Allah and with His praise."
"9792","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Beware of wisal (continuous fasting), he said it three times, they said: But you perform wisal? He said: Who among you is like me in that? Indeed I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink, so burden yourselves of deeds what you can bear. And some of these hadiths have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles, and some none narrated except Abu Zur'ah; as for what none narrated except Abu Zur'ah from Abu Hurayrah: Give glad tidings to Khadijah, and his saying: Two words light upon the tongue, then these two hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Abu Hurayrah except Abu Zur'ah."
"9793","And Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sustenance. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9794","Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abdillah ibn Bishr al-Khath'ami, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended travel would say: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel, and the Successor over the family, O Allah, accompany us with success - thus I think it, or similar to this wording - and return us with protection, O Allah, fold the earth for us and ease travel for us, O Allah, indeed I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel and the gloom of return. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah with this wording except from this angle."
"9795","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir and Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Talq ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9796","And Yusuf narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has three children die - I think he said: - who had not reached puberty, the Fire will not touch him."
"9797","Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the severity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool (delay) prayer in severe heat. Meaning the Zuhr prayer. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Umarah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Sharik."
"9798","Sa'id ibn Nuh and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not parted. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Zur'ah except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"9799","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9800","He said: And Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to me, from Shahr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three: witr before sleep, the two rak'ahs of al-Duha, and fasting three days of every month. And the hadith of Shahr from Abu Hurayrah was narrated by more than one from Shahr, while the hadith of Yahya ibn Ayyub, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya except Muhammad ibn Yusuf."
"9801","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah that a prophet among the prophets alighted under a tree and an ant stung him, so he commanded the tree and it was burned - meaning with what was in it of ants - so Allah revealed to him: Why not one ant in place of ants? He said: And I think he raised it (to the Prophet)."
"9802","Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Bujayr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Jarir ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."
"9803","And with his chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two leather socks. And Jarir ibn Ayyub is not a preserver."
"9804","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir - meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid - narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9805","And Yusuf narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Harith al-Ukli, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, they said: Abu Hurayrah said: I shall never cease loving Banu Tamim after three things I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about them, he said: They are the sternest of my Ummah against the Dajjal. And A'ishah had to free a slave from the children of Ismail, and captives came from them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free this one - meaning one of them - for indeed she is from the children of Ismail. And their charities came, so he said: These are the charities of our people."
"9806","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is that you give it while you are healthy and miserly, hoping for life and fearing poverty, and do not delay until when it reaches the throat you say: For so-and-so such-and-such, though it already belongs to so-and-so. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Zur'ah from Abu Hurayrah."
"9807","And Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pause between the takbir and the recitation briefly. So I said: By my father and mother, have you seen your pauses between the takbir and the recitation, what do you say in them? He said: I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west, O Allah, purify me of my sins as the white garment is purified of filth, O Allah, wash me of my sins with snow and hail and cold water. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Abu Zur'ah."
"9808","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' and Ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, they said: Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted has guaranteed for whoever goes out striving in the path of Allah, nothing brings him out except faith in Me and belief in My Messenger, that I shall admit him to Paradise or return him to his home from which he went out, attaining what he attained of reward and booty. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no Muslim wounded in the path of Allah except he comes on the Day of Resurrection with his wound bleeding, the colour the colour of blood and the scent the scent of musk. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would not have stayed behind from any expedition fighting in the path of Allah, and I do not find what to carry them upon, nor do they find means to follow me, nor would their souls be content to stay behind after me. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I wish I would fight in the path of Allah and be killed, then fight and be killed, then fight and be killed."
"9809","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A bowl of tharid and meat was placed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the most beloved of sheep to him was the foreleg, so he took a bite, he said: I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection. When his companions saw that he said: Will you not say how? They said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: People will stand before the Lord of the worlds, the caller makes them hear, and the sight reaches them, and the sun draws near their heads, and its heat intensifies upon them, and its nearness to them burdens them, and weariness and anguish reach them from what they are in, so they come to Adam - peace be upon him - and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, Allah created you with His Hand, and breathed into you of His spirit, and commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, will you not intercede for us to our Lord? Do you not see what evil we are in? So Adam will say: Indeed my Lord the Blessed and Exalted has angered today an anger like which He never angered before it and never will anger after it, and He commanded me with a command and I disobeyed Him and obeyed Satan; He forbade me from eating the tree and I disobeyed Him, so I fear He will cast me into the Fire, go to other than me, myself myself. So they go to Nuh, peace be upon him, and say: O Nuh, you are the prophet of Allah, and the first one sent, intercede for us to your Lord, do you not see what evil we are in? So Nuh will say: Indeed my Lord the Blessed and Exalted has angered today an anger like which He never angered before it and never will anger after it, and I had a supplication and I supplicated with it against my people and they were destroyed, and indeed I fear He will cast me into the Fire, go to other than me, myself myself. So they go to Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and say: O Ibrahim, you are the close friend of Allah, the people of the heavens and the people of the earth have heard of your close friendship, intercede for us to your Lord, do you not see what evil we are in? So he will say: Indeed my Lord the Blessed and Exalted has angered today an anger like which He never angered before it and never will anger after it, and indeed I fear He will cast me into the Fire. And he mentioned his saying about the star: This is my Lord, and his saying: Rather the eldest of them did this, and his saying: Indeed I am sick, go to other than me, myself myself. So they go to Musa, peace be upon him, and say: O Musa, you are the prophet of Allah, Allah chose you with His messages and spoke to you directly, intercede for us to your Lord, do you not see what evil we are in? So Musa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will say: Indeed my Lord the Blessed and Exalted has angered today an anger like which He never angered before it and never will anger after it, and indeed I killed a soul I was not commanded to, I fear He will cast me into the Fire, go to other than me, myself myself. So they go to Isa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and say: O Isa, you are the prophet of Allah and His word and His spirit which He cast to Maryam, intercede for us to your Lord, do you not see what evil we are in? So he will say: Indeed my Lord has angered today an anger like which He never angered before it and never will anger after it, and indeed I fear He will cast me into the Fire - Umarah said: And I do not know he mentioned a sin - go to other than me, myself myself. So they come to me and say: You are the Messenger of Allah and the seal of the prophets, Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed, intercede for us to your Lord. So I go and come beneath the Throne and fall prostrating to my Lord the Blessed and Exalted, then I rise from it to a station none before me stood and none after me shall stand, so He says: O Muhammad, intercede and you shall be granted intercession, and ask and you shall be given. So I say: My Ummah, O Lord, my Ummah. So He says: O Muhammad, admit those upon whom there is no reckoning through the right gate, and they are partners of people in the other gates, so by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, indeed what is between the gate is farther than what is between Busra and Makkah, or Makkah and Hajar. Umarah said: I do not know which of the two he said. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Umarah except Jarir."
"9810","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman informed me, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A son of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, grew heavy (ill), so she sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return, for to Him belongs what He took and to Him belongs what He left, and all is for a decreed term. When he was dying she sent to him and he said to us: Stand. When he sat he began reciting: {Then why, when it reaches the throat * while you at that time look on}, until he passed away. So the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, you weep and forbid weeping! He said: It is only mercy, and Allah only has mercy upon the merciful among His servants. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Umarah from Abu Zur'ah except Ismail ibn Muslim, though al-A'mash and al-Thawri and a group narrated from Ismail, yet he is not a preserver."
"9811","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, who among people most deserves my good companionship? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your father, then the nearest then the nearest."
"9812","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The blood of a Muslim person is not lawful except by one of three: adultery after chastity, or disbelief after Islam, or one who kills a soul deliberately, so he is killed for it."
"9813","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' and Ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he rose in the second - meaning of the prayer - would begin with {Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds} and would not pause. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Yahya ibn Hassan from Abd al-Wahid, and I think he shortened it from a hadith."
"9814","Ishaq ibn Buhlul and Muhammad ibn al-Mustanir narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what is Allah's right upon the servants? Mu'adh said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: His right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what is the servants' right upon Allah when they worship Him and associate nothing with Him? Mu'adh said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Their right upon Him is that He admits them to Paradise. Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go to the people and give them glad tidings? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, leave them to work. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9815","Abdillah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Jibril sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, indeed this angel has not descended since the day he was created, and when he descended he said: O Muhammad, indeed I am your Lord's messenger to you, between that your Lord makes you a king or a servant messenger? So Jibril said to him: Be humble to your Lord, O Muhammad. He said: A servant messenger. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9816","Abu Khalid from him: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me last night and admitted me to Paradise, and showed me the gate through which I and my Ummah shall enter. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I wish I had been with you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he took his hand and said: I and you are the first of my Ummah to enter through it. And we do not know it to be narrated except from this angle with this chain."
"9817","Kathir: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Kathir Abu al-Anbas narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I think he raised it, who said: There shall surely come upon people a time when a man goes to his brother's grave and places his hand upon his grave and says: Would that I were in your place and had not seen what I see."
"9818","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abu al-Anbas - meaning Sa'id ibn Kathir - narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they testify that there is no god but Allah, and establish prayer and give zakat, and when they do that, their blood and wealth become forbidden to me, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"9819","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham meaning Ibn Abi Abdillah narrated to us, from Hajjaj - meaning Ibn Artah - from Salit - and he is Ibn Abdillah - from Dhuhl ibn Awf al-Taymi, and it is said: he is Dhuhayl ibn Awf ibn al-Shammakh, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for one of us of his brother's wealth? He said: He eats and does not carry, and drinks and does not carry. And we do not know that Dhuhayl ibn Awf narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9820","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, Hafs ibn Umar and Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, they said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, and the wording is Musa's, from al-Hajjaj, from Salit ibn Abdillah, from Dhuhayl ibn Awf ibn Shammakh, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, when we came upon camels tied with tree bark, so we scattered among them milking them, then it was announced among us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Indeed these camels belong to a Muslim household, and in their udders is their sustenance, so do not milk them except with their owners' permission. So a man said: So what belongs to one of us of his brother's wealth when commanded with it? He said: He eats and drinks and does not carry."
"9821","Abu Iyad: Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Hajari - meaning Ibrahim - from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The day of Ashura is the festival of a prophet before you, so fast it yourselves."
"9822","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah. And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Ibrahim - meaning al-Hajari - from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am only a human who angers as humans anger and is pleased as humans are pleased, so whichever servant I curse without its essence, make it for him a prayer and reward, or a prayer and mercy."
"9823","Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim - meaning al-Hajari - from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Nothing remains of prophethood except the righteous servant's dream, and it is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"9824","Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us - as far as I know - he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Hajari, from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every Muslim every day is charity. So a man said: Who can bear this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your removing harm from the road is charity, and your guiding a man the road is charity, and your visiting the sick is charity, and your following the funeral is charity, and your enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity, and a Muslim's returning greeting to a Muslim is charity."
"9825","Ibrahim narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid - meaning Ibn Abdillah - narrated to us, al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of knowledge that does not benefit is like the likeness of treasure not spent in the path of Allah."
"9826","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Hajjaj, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail or Ismail ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you prays, let him not perform voluntary prayer in his place, but let him move forward or backward, or to his right or to his left. And perhaps he said: Is one of you unable to move forward. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain, and this Hajjaj is Hajjaj ibn Ubayd."
"9827","Ibn Abi Nu'm from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Nu'm saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the prostitute, and the price of the dog, and the stud fee of the stallion. And Abu Hurayrah said: These are from my own store."
"9828","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Nu'm narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Gold for gold, and silver for silver, like for like, weight for weight, so whoever adds, then it is usury."
"9829","Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham informed us, from Sufyan, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever slanders his slave while he is innocent of what he said will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said. And we do not know it to be narrated with this wording from Abu Hurayrah with this chain."
"9830","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Awfi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Teach your children prayer when they reach seven, and strike them for it when they reach ten, and separate them in beds. And we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9831","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah, Ayyub from Muhammad: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two afternoon prayers - he said: And my strongest thought is that it was Zuhr - then he went to a piece of wood in the mosque and placed his hands upon it, one upon the other, and the hasty people left saying: The prayer has been shortened. And among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, and they feared to speak to him, so a man stood, either short-handed or long-handed, called Dhu al-Yadayn, and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: It was not shortened nor did I forget? He said: Rather you forgot. So he said: Has Dhu al-Yadayn spoken truth? They said: Yes. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us two rak'ahs then gave salam, then said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said takbir. He said: And I was informed from Imran ibn Husayn, that he said: Then he gave salam. And a group narrated this hadith from Ayyub, and more than one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin."
"9832","And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam. And Qatadah, Ibn Awn, Asim al-Ahwal, Qurrah ibn Khalid, Hisham ibn Hassan, and others narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah."
"9833","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man stood to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: And do all of you find two garments? And Hammad ibn Zayd, Ibn Ulayyah, Hammad ibn Salamah, and Ma'mar narrated this hadith from Ayyub. And a group of trustworthy narrators narrated it from Ibn Sirin."
"9834","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: None of you shall be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him. And more than one trustworthy narrator narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah."
"9835","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When time draws near, a Muslim's dream hardly lies, and the truest of them in dream is the truest of them - I think he said: in speech - and a Muslim's dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood, and dreams are three: from them glad tidings from Allah, and a dream of grief from Satan, and a dream of what a person speaks to himself about, so when one of you sees what he dislikes, let him stand and pray and not narrate it to people, and he loves the shackle (qayd), and dislikes the collar (ghull), and the shackle is firmness in religion. And a group narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah."
"9836","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves by my name and do not take my kunyah. And Ma'mar also narrated this hadith from Ayyub."
"9837","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah. And more than one narrated it from Ibn Sirin, and it was also narrated from other than Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9838","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Aslam, may Allah grant them safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them."
"9839","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines, so the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they understand. And Ma'mar narrated this hadith from Ayyub with the like of Abd al-Wahhab's narration, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9840","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade two garments: that a man sit with knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it covering his private part, and that he wrap himself in the garment from beneath his elbows - I think he said: upon his shoulder - and (he forbade) two sales: limas and nabidh."
"9841","Yahya ibn Hakim narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: They used to forbid the sale of nibadh and limas. He said: And nibadh is that he tosses - meaning the thing - to another, and limas is that he brings out the edge of his garment."
"9842","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade ikhtisar, meaning in prayer. And we do not know Ayyub raised it, while Hisham and others raised it."
"9843","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Sulayman ibn Dawud had such-and-such women, so he said: I shall surely go around them tonight and every woman among them shall bear a boy who fights in the path of Allah. He said: So he went around them, and none of them conceived except one woman, they say half a human, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But had he made exception, every woman among them would have borne a boy who fights in the path of Allah. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles."
"9844","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim - meaning Ibn Ulayyah - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah are better than the two allies; Asad and Ghatfan and Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah, they have failed and lost. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles."
"9845","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed me, he said: Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call grapes karm."
"9846","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the best charity is what is from sufficiency. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Ma'mar."
"9847","And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Repentance continues to be accepted as long as the sun has not risen from its west."
"9848","And al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abbad Abu Abbad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And more than one narrated this hadith from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ma'mar and Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"9849","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9850","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the wording is Abd al-Wahhab's, he said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour no Muslim standing praying asking Allah therein for good meets it except He gives it to him. Then he gestured with his hand minimizing it, making it slight. And more than one narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah, and it was narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles."
"9851","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you is invited, let him answer, and if he is fasting, let him pray (make supplication)."
"9852","And al-Husayn narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of Yemen have come to you, softest hearts; faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni."
"9853","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."
"9854","And Muhammad ibn Umarah and Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated it to us, they said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Allah the Blessed and Exalted has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."
"9855","And Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of one's vessel when the dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first with dust. And this hadith has been narrated from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from other angles, and al-Mu'tamir narrated it from Ayyub, adding the story of the cat, while others besides al-Mu'tamir raised it, making the washing for the cat once from the saying of Abu Hurayrah, though Qurrah narrated it raised."
"9856","And Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"9857","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Abbad informed me, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse time, for indeed Allah is Time. And more than one narrated this hadith raised from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah."
"9858","Muhammad ibn Abi Madh'ur narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you points at his brother with iron, the angels curse him until he puts it down, even if he is his full brother. And we do not know anyone who narrated it raised from Ayyub except Ibn Uyaynah."
"9859","Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: What do you count the martyr among you? They said: Being killed in the path of Allah. He said: Indeed the martyrs of my Ummah would then be few; being killed is martyrdom, and drowning is martyrdom, and the woman killed by her child (in childbirth) is martyrdom. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Tufawi alone."
"9860","And Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt, and a woman should not ask for her sister's divorce to empty what is in her bowl. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Tufawi."
"9861","With his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have been given the openings of speech and I have been aided with terror, and while I was sleeping last night I was brought the keys of the treasuries of the earth - I think he said - Abu Hurayrah said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while you are taking them out. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Tufawi."
"9862","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Fire and Paradise disputed, so the Fire said: The tyrants and the arrogant will enter me. And Paradise said: The weak and lowly among people will enter me. So He said to the Fire: You are My punishment, I afflict with you whomever I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy, I bestow with you upon whomever I will. Then on the Day of Resurrection people will be thrown into the Fire and it will say: Is there any more? Until He places His foot in it, then it will shrink and say: Enough, enough. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Tufawi."
"9863","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Adam and Musa argued, so Musa said: O Adam, you whom Allah created with His hand, and settled you in His Paradise, and made His angels prostrate to you, and you took people out of Paradise and made them wretched. So Adam said: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His speech and His messages, and sent down upon you the Torah, so do you find in the Torah that He wrote it upon me before He created me? He said: Yes. He said: Then Adam defeated Musa in argument. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah and Asim ibn Hilal."
"9864","Salamah ibn Shabib and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, and the wording is Salamah's, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that they boasted one day in his presence, and said: Are men more in Paradise or women? So Abu Hurayrah said: Did not Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first group to enter Paradise, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon, then those who follow them like the brightest brilliant star in the sky, for each man among them two wives, the marrow of her leg seen from behind the flesh, and by Him in Whose hand is my soul, there is no unmarried person in it. And Hammad ibn Salamah also narrated this hadith from Ayyub and others, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9865","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The vessel is washed seven times, the first of them with dust."
"9866","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes - meaning to the prayer - let him not hasten to it, and let him walk with calmness and dignity, then let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"9867","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that he prostrated in [When the sky splits open], and said: One better than me prostrated in it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in it."
"9868","And Muammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: People will keep asking about knowledge until they say: This is Allah Who created us, so who created Allah? Abu Hurayrah said: After the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), two men have asked me, and this is the third."
"9869","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated it to us, he said: Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People will keep asking about knowledge... then he mentioned similar to it."
"9870","Salamah ibn Shabib and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys a musarrah animal, he milks it, then if he is pleased with it he keeps it, otherwise he returns it along with a saa of dates. And Hammad ibn Salamah also narrated this hadith from Ayyub and others, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9871","Maymun ibn al-Asbagh narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man will meet his father on the Day of Resurrection and say: O father, will you obey me today, or will you benefit me today? He will say: Yes. So he takes his hand and goes with him until he brings him to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He is presenting the creation, and he says: O Lord, You promised me You would not disgrace me, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, turns away from him, then he says the like of that, then Allah transforms his father into a hyena, and he falls into the Fire, and he says: Your father? And he says: I do not know you. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9872","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels send blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place: O Allah forgive him, O Allah have mercy on him, as long as he remains in his prayer place waiting for the prayer."
"9873","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father Abd al-Warith ibn Said, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam, and those after him act upon it, he will have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it, without anything being diminished from their rewards. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Warith. And Hisham narrated it from Muhammad, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his father."
"9874","Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man's messenger to a man is his permission."
"9875","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated it to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah, and Ibn Mahdi narrated it from Hammad, from Habib, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah; Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us from Abd al-Rahman."
"9876","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham and Habib, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9877","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9878","And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated it to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let none of you urinate in stagnant water and then bathe from it."
"9879","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not leave camels and sheep unmilked (to deceive buyers)."
"9880","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham and Habib, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub and Habib except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9881","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever eats forgetfully, then Allah has fed him and given him drink. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub and Habib except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9882","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, except al-Harith ibn Umayr."
"9883","Al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Rukhami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bilal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report, he said: A woman was forgiven who passed by a panting dog and gave it water."
"9884","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning and differing with their prophets, so when I forbid you something avoid it, and when I command you with something, do of it - I think he said - what you are able."
"9885","And Muhammad narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9886","Yusuf ibn Musa and the nephew of Hannad narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us, Rabah ibn Amr al-Basri narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a youth came upon us from a mountain pass, and when he drew near us we said: If only this youth would use his youth and strength in the path of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard our words and said: And what is the path of Allah except one who is killed? Whoever strives for his parents is in the path of Allah, and whoever strives to boast is in the path of the false deity. And this hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Rabah ibn Amr, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Rabah except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"9887","Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Tahhan narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters except he chose the easier of them. And I do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Sahl ibn Ziyad, and he is a Basran man whom more than one of the people of Basra narrated from, there is no harm in him, and he was not followed in this hadith."
"9888","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Muqri wrote to me informing that his father Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to him from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever has them is a hypocrite, even if he fasts and prays and claims he is a believer: when he speaks he lies, when he is trusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks it. And others than al-Muqri narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Dawud, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I think al-Muqri erred in it."
"9889","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"9890","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report, he said: Love your beloved moderately, perhaps he will be hateful to you one day, and hate whom you hate moderately, perhaps he will be beloved to you one day. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain with this chain of transmission, and we heard it only from Abu Kurayb, and al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated it from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ali. And likewise Harun al-Ahwazi narrated it from Muhammad, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, and that is the correct one."
"9891","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Ibn Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people and took off his sandals, and when the people perceived it they took off their sandals, and when he finished his prayer he turned to the people and said: An angel came to me and informed me that there was filth on my sandals, so when one of you comes to the mosque let him turn over his sandals, and if he sees anything on them let him wipe them then pray in them. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abbad ibn Kathir, and he is weak in hadith, and none narrated it from Abbad except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"9892","Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah I would not have narrated to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he recited: [Those who conceal what We sent down of clear proofs and guidance after We made it clear] the verse."
"9893","Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd and Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him walk in his usual manner, then let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hushaym."
"9894","And I saw in another place in my notes from him, from Hushaym, from Yunus and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"9895","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Abu Hammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels send blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place: O Allah forgive him, O Allah have mercy on him, as long as he does not break his ablution."
"9896","Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated it to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9897","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, Abu Khalaf Abd Allah ibn Isa narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in stagnant water."
"9898","Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ayli narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus and Hisham and Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two afternoon prayers and gave salam after two rakahs, then went out to a crossbeam in the mosque and the hasty people went out, then a man called Dhu al-Yadayn stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: It has neither been shortened nor did I forget. He said: You gave salam after two rakahs. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says? They said: Yes. So he returned and prayed two rakahs, then made tashahhud, then gave salam and prostrated two prostrations."
"9899","And Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated it to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham and Yunus - I think he said - and Humayd and others, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9900","And we do not preserve this hadith from the hadith of Yunus except from Hammad ibn Salamah, except for an elder who was with us in Basra, nicknamed Abu Muhammad, who was a hadith scholar, who narrated it from his father, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9901","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani and Harun ibn Musa al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal while he had a pile of dates, and said: What is this? He said: I am storing it. He said: Do you not fear seeing its vapor in the fire of Hell? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Owner of the Throne. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"9902","Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar Abu Bakr al-Bukhari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yunus - meaning Ibn Ubayd - from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer at three times: when the sun rises until it rises high, and when it sets until it sets, and at midday. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ubayd Allah ibn Amr."
"9903","Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Isa narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the perfection of faith is good character. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Abd Allah ibn Isa, and he was not a memorizer, and he used to be with Yunus ibn Ubayd in his shop, and a group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"9904","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The women of Paradise, the marrow of their legs is seen from behind the flesh. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9905","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog licks a vessel, wash it seven times, the first of them or the last of them with dust. Bundar narrated this hadith thus, and others narrated it from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Ibrahim ibn Sadaqah."
"9906","Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Abu Khalaf narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The dream of the believing servant is one part of forty parts of prophethood."
"9907","And Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated it to us, Abu Khalaf Abd Allah ibn Isa narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When time draws near, the dream of the believer hardly lies, and I love the shackle and dislike the yoke. He said: And I do not know except that he raised it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9908","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan and Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prayer in a single garment, he said: And do all of you find two garments? And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Hushaym."
"9909","Jabir ibn al-Kurdi narrated to us, as far as I know, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarrah animal has the choice of one of two considerations; if he returns it, he returns with it a saa, not samra (a type of wheat). And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Hushaym."
"9910","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazia narrated to us, Fadalah ibn Husayn al-Attar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal until he fixes the other. Thus we saw this hadith in the book of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, from Fadalah, he said: And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus except Fadalah ibn Husayn, and he is a well-known man from the people of Basra."
"9911","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"9912","And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report with similar to it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Anbasah, and we heard it only from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl, from his father."
"9913","Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of the hadith of Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said, that he said: The people of the Fire will be thrown into it and it will say: Is there any more? As for Paradise, there will remain of it what Allah wills, then Allah will create a creation for it and settle them in it."
"9914","And Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated to us, Yunus and Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus and Hisham except al-Aghlab, and we heard it only from Abu al-Khattab, and al-Aghlab was not a memorizer, and Zayd ibn al-Hubab and others of our companions narrated from him."
"9915","Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Qulusi narrated to us, whose origin was Baghdadi but he settled in Basra, he said: Bayan ibn Humran narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, Ayyub and Yunus and Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you is invited, let him accept, then if he wishes he eats and if he wishes he leaves. And we do not preserve it from the hadith of Yunus except from Bayan, from Mufaddal, and we heard it only from Ishaq."
"9916","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, who said: Abu Hurayrah said, he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour no Muslim servant coincides with asking Allah for good in it except He gives it to him."
"9917","And with his chain he said: Abu Hurayrah said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, except that Allah envelops me with forgiveness and mercy from Him. And Ibn Awn placed his palm on his head describing the action of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9918","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two afternoon prayers; he prayed two rakahs then gave salam, then stood to a beam displayed in the mosque, and placed his hand upon it - and Ibn Awn described that he placed one of his hands upon the other, and placed his hand upon it as if angry - then the hasty ones went out of the doors of the mosque, and said: The prayer has been shortened, and among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar but they feared to speak to him, and among the people was a long-handed man called Dhu al-Yadayn, who said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: I neither forgot nor was it shortened. And he said: Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says? They said: Yes. So he returned and prayed what he had left, then gave salam, then said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said takbir then prostrated. Ibn Awn said: And Muhammad would sometimes say: And I was informed from Imran ibn Husayn that he said: Then he gave salam."
"9919","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you, softest in hearts; faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"9920","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, who said: I think it is from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man called out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: And do all of you find two garments?"
"9921","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the delegation of Abd al-Qays: I forbid you dubba, naqir, muqayyar, hantam, and the cut-off waterskin, but drink in your waterskin and tie it."
"9922","And Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn except Nuh ibn Qays."
"9923","Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Tai and Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as he waits for the prayer."
"9924","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels send blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, in raised form, except Abd al-Qahir."
"9925","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Imran narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Repentance continues to be accepted as long as the sun has not risen from its west. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, in raised form, except Abd Allah ibn Humran."
"9926","Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalifah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9927","And Harun ibn Musa al-Mustamli narrated it to us, Mansur ibn Ikrimah narrated to us, Hisham and Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Adam and Musa disputed, so Musa said to him: You are Adam who made people wretched and took them out of Paradise. So Adam said: Are you Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His words, and sent down upon you the Torah? He said: Yes. He said: Then did you find that He decreed that upon me before He created me? He said: Yes. He said: Then Adam defeated Musa in argument, then Adam defeated Musa in argument - three times. And the wording is the wording of Mansur ibn Ikrimah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with a connected chain from Ibn Awn except Yahya ibn Khalifah and Mansur ibn Ikrimah."
"9928","Ibrahim ibn Said, Rizq Allah ibn Musa, and Tulayq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat intensifies, cool down from the prayer, for intense heat is from the blast of Hell. And this hadith is known through Ishaq as having narrated it with a connected chain, and Yazid ibn Harun followed him and combined Ibn Awn and Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, in this hadith, and I think Yazid carried the hadith of Ibn Awn upon the hadith of Hisham because it is famous through Ishaq."
"9929","Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Darir al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham and Ibn Awn informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited, let him accept, and if he is fasting let him supplicate. And we heard this hadith only from Muhammad ibn Ismail from Yazid, and we do not know anyone who followed him in it."
"9930","Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad Abu al-Rabia narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Uryan narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out for prayer, and when the rows were straightened he gestured to them with his hand, then entered and returned with his head dripping, then prayed with them. And we heard this hadith only from Abu al-Rabia, and he was trustworthy and reliable."
"9931","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Baghdadi and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham and Ibn Awn informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels curse one of you when he points at his brother with a piece of iron, even if he is his full brother through his father and mother. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn except Yazid ibn Harun with a connected chain."
"9932","And Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report, he said: Let none of you urinate in stagnant water, or he forbade urinating in stagnant water."
"9933","Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, Mansur ibn Ikrimah narrated to us, Hisham and Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with a connected chain from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mansur ibn Ikrimah."
"9934","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse time, for Allah is time. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with a connected chain from Ibn Awn except Mansur ibn Ikrimah, and it is well-known as raised through Hisham and others."
"9935","Muhammad ibn Amrawayh Abu Abd Allah al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: Ashhal ibn Hatim narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call grapes karm, for karm is the Muslim. And we do not preserve it from the hadith of Ibn Awn except from Ashhal, and we heard it only from Abu Abd Allah, and he was trustworthy, and he was praised with good."
"9936","Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, Mansur ibn Ikrimah narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is written for him, and whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, it is not written against him, but if he does it, one evil deed is written against him. And we do not preserve it from the hadith of Ibn Awn except from Mansur from him, and we heard it only from Harun ibn Musa."
"9937","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Abd Allah al-Sirini narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me things I will never abandon: fasting three days of every month, bathing on Friday, and not sleeping except upon witr. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn except Bakkar, and he narrated hadiths from Ibn Awn upon which he was not followed."
"9938","Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ayli narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal while he had a pile of wealth - or he said dates - and said: Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Owner of the Throne. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn except Bakkar."
"9939","Ishaq ibn Sayyar al-Nasibi narrated to us, Awn ibn Umarah narrated to us, Ibn Awn and al-Rabia ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt nor her maternal aunt, a man does not propose over the proposal of his brother, nor does he outbid him. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn, nor from al-Rabia ibn Subayh, except Awn ibn Umarah, and he was not followed in it, though it is well-known from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah. And Ayyub, Hisham, Yunus and a group narrated this hadith from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, and it was only criticized from the hadith of Ibn Awn and al-Rabia ibn Subayh since this hadith is not known from their hadith except through Awn ibn Umarah, and Awn ibn Umarah was Basran; he narrated from Hisham ibn Hassan from al-Hasan, he said: The greeting suffices as permission. And this has no basis from Hisham from al-Hasan; I heard Amr ibn Ali say: It reached me that he narrates this hadith from Hisham from al-Hasan, so I came to him and asked him about it and he mentioned it, and I wanted to complain against him but they spoke to me about him, and said: He is a weak elder, so I left him, though a group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith, and I do not think these hadiths criticized against him are except from his poor memory, not that he intended it."
"9940","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Awf and Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him come with calmness upon him, then let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed or what he lost. And Ayyub, Hisham and Awf narrated this hadith, and it was only appreciated from the hadith of Ibn Awn due to the eminence of Ibn Awn, and the number of hadiths he narrated with connected chains."
"9941","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Wajih informed us, Malik ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Under every hair is ritual impurity, so wet the hair and clean the skin. And we do not know Malik narrated with a connected chain from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Malik except al-Harith ibn Wajih."
"9942","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Minjab narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind - meaning al-Shaabi - and Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt nor her maternal aunt. And a group narrated this hadith from Dawud, from al-Shaabi, from Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know anyone who combined from Dawud from al-Shaabi and Muhammad except Ali ibn Mushir, and Dawud did not narrate with a connected chain from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah other than this hadith."
"9943","Muhammad ibn al-Ala Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: And do all of you find two garments?"
"9944","And Abu al-Saib Salm ibn Junadah narrated it to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal and others, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9945","And Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated it to us, Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, and Hammad ibn Salamah also narrated it; Abu Musa narrated it to us from Hajjaj, from Hammad."
"9946","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. And he did not raise it."
"9947","And Salamah ibn Shabib and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, they said: Al-Faryabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with a connected chain from Asim except al-Faryabi from Sufyan."
"9948","And Bishr ibn Muadh and Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated to us, they said: Al-Sakan ibn Ismail narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Umar, they raised the hadith, one of them from Umar and the other from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He forbade muzaffat made from skins, and one of them said: The earthen jar, and the other said: Pottery. And others than Asim narrated this hadith from Ibn Sirin."
"9949","And Abd Allah ibn Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two afternoon prayers two rakahs then gave salam, then the hasty people rushed out and said: The prayer has been shortened. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to a pillar and placed his hand upon it, and anger was recognized on his face, and among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar but they feared to speak to him, then Dhu al-Yadayn said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: It has neither been shortened nor did I know I forgot. He said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. So he said to the people, and they said: He spoke the truth. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his place and prayed two rakahs, then gave salam to his right and left, and prostrated two prostrations, and sat a little; Asim said: Abu Qilabah said: Then he gave salam. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim except al-Muharibi."
"9950","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Abu Said al-Jufi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him come with calmness upon him, then let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with a connected chain from Asim except Ali ibn Mushir."
"9951","And Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A grazing animal killed is of no liability, a well is of no liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth. And he did not narrate it with a connected chain. And others than Abu Kurayb narrated this hadith with a connected chain from Abu Muawiyah."
"9952","Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisia narrated to us, Abu Qatan narrated to us, Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked: Does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurrah except Abu Qatan, and the name of Abu Hurrah is Wasil ibn Abd al-Rahman, and the name of Abu Qatan is Amr ibn al-Haytham."
"9953","And Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Salm ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report, he said: When time draws near, the dream of the Muslim hardly lies, and the truest of them in dream is the truest of them in speech, and dreams are three: a glad tiding from Allah, a dream from what a man tells himself, and a saddening dream from Satan."
"9954","And Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Salm ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The dream of the believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. And we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Abu Hurrah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, concerning dreams, except Salm ibn Sulayman, and its narrator from Abu Hurrah was unobjectionable."
"9955","Ishaq ibn Hatim al-Allaf, a Baghdadi, narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan, Abu Hurrah Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, al-Salt ibn Dinar, Sahl ibn Bistamm, and al-Rabia ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? And we do not know Sahl narrated with a connected chain from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, other than this hadith, and we heard it only from Ishaq from Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"9956","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, Salm - meaning Ibn Abi al-Dhiyal - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? And we do not know Salm narrated with a connected chain from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9957","Nasr ibn Ali, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and Amr ibn Isa al-Dubai narrated to us, and the wording is Amr's, they said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, except Abd al-Ala, from Said."
"9958","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Isa al-Dubai narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog licks a vessel, it is washed seven times, the last with dust. And a group narrated this hadith from Qatadah, among them: Said ibn Abi Arubah, Aban ibn Yazid, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik, Khulayd ibn Dalaj, and Said ibn Bashir."
"9959","As for the hadith of Aban: Muhammad ibn Marzuq and Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And as for the hadith of al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik:"
"9960","Al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9961","And as for the hadith of Said ibn Bashir: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9962","And as for the hadith of Khulayd ibn Dalaj: Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9963","Ahmad ibn Abi Ubayd Allah Abu Abd Allah al-Warraq narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When time draws near, the dream of the believer hardly lies, and the truest of them in dream is the truest of them in speech, and dreams are three: a dream from what a man tells himself, a true dream, and a saddening dream from Satan, and I love the shackle and dislike the yoke, so when one of you sees what he dislikes, let him stand and pray."
"9964","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9965","And from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9966","And al-Fadl ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The dream of the believer is one part of forty-five, or a few and forty parts of prophethood. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Ubayd Allah ibn Amr."
"9967","Muhammad ibn Marzuq, Muhammad ibn Mamar, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."
"9968","And Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it."
"9969","And Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to the hadith of Said, and he recited this verse: [And to Allah belong the most beautiful names, so call upon Him by them]."
"9970","Abd Allah ibn Said Abu Said narrated to us, Abu Khalid, meaning Sulayman ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any fasting person who eats or drinks forgetfully should not break his fast, for it is only provision Allah provided him."
"9971","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats while fasting, then Allah has fed him and given him drink. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah and Said ibn Bashir."
"9972","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the cooking pots on the day of Khaybar to be overturned, so we overturned them. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Hammam, and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Musa, and others than Qatadah narrate it from Ibn Sirin from Anas."
"9973","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah or Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to the prayer, come with calmness upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, make up."
"9974","And Muhammad ibn Marzuq, Ahmad ibn Mualla al-Adami, and Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women. Meaning: in prayer. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Aban, nor from Aban except Musa."
"9975","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim and Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Ayli narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hell sought permission from its Lord to breathe twice every year; so intense heat is from its blast, and intense cold is from its freezing cold. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik."
"9976","Al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you, softest in hearts; faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except al-Hakam, and we heard it only from al-Husayn ibn Ali from Ali ibn Thabit."
"9977","Yahya ibn al-Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Paradise and the Fire disputed, so the Fire said: The arrogant will enter me. And Paradise said: None will enter me except the weak and poor. So Allah revealed to them that each one of them will have its fill; the people of the Fire will be thrown into it and it will say: Is there any more? And they will be thrown into it and it will say: Is there any more? Then the Blessed and Exalted will place His foot in it and it will shrink, and as for Paradise, much of it will remain, so Allah will create a creation for it. And this hadith is not preserved from the hadith of Qatadah except from Said ibn Bashir."
"9978","Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yahya, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let none of you say my slave or my slave-girl, but let him say: my youth and my maiden. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the hadith of Qatadah from Muhammad except from the hadith of Said ibn Bashir from him."
"9979","Ahmad ibn Abd Allah Abu Bakr al-Bilali narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Jad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarrah animal has the choice; if he wishes he keeps it, and if he returns it he returns with it a saa of wheat, not samra."
"9980","Ahmad ibn Abd Allah Abu Bakr narrated to us, Jafar ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Jad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A mine is of no liability, a well is of no liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"9981","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A mine is of no liability, a well is of no liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth. And we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of musarrah except Hammad ibn al-Jad."
"9982","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih wrote to me, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn after the salam. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Amr ibn al-Harith, and Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin himself."
"9983","And Muhammad ibn al-Aswad al-Ammi narrated it to us with it, Ibrahim ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the story of Dhu al-Yadayn."
"9984","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, and I found it written in my notes in my handwriting, he said: Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, from Said - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me, then it is me, for Satan cannot take my likeness. And he used to say: Dreams are not related except to a scholar or a sincere adviser. And we do not preserve this hadith from the hadith of Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from anyone, and I saw it in another place from Hisham from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah."
"9985","Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Qattan al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Nasr ibn Abi Nasr narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two kinds of wearing, and prayer at two times: prayer when the sun rises, meaning until it rises high, and when it sets until it sets, and that a man wraps himself in a single garment with nothing of it upon his private part, and the other has left my mind."
"9986","And Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Nasr narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it. And this Ibn Abi Nasr is in my view Nasr ibn Tarif, whose hadith was abandoned, and he was from the people of Basra, well-known."
"9987","Amr ibn Bishr narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Bayan narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage belongs to whoever paid the price. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain, and Shuayb was not followed in his narration from Imran."
"9988","And Muhammad ibn Salih Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Bashir, narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) did not lie except three lies; two concerning the essence of Allah, Exalted: His saying: [Rather, the eldest of them did it], [He looked a glance at the stars, then said: I am sick], and he passed by a tyrant while his wife was with him, so he said: Say he is my brother, for I am your brother and you are my sister; there is no believer on earth other than us, fearing he would overpower him for her if he said she is my wife. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except Imran, nor from Imran except Said ibn Bashir."
"9989","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, he said: al-Muthanna and Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn two prostrations; the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"9990","And Muhammad narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar to it. And Ibn Wahb narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith. And as for the hadith of Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Amr ibn al-Harith, this, we heard it only from Ibn [...]."
"9991","From Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say my slave or my slave-girl, and let not the owned say my lord and my lady, but let the owner say: my youth and my maiden, and let the owned say: my master and my mistress, for you are all owned and the Lord is Allah."
"9992","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse time, for Allah is time."
"9993","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"9994","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The mouse is Jewish; do you not see that it does not drink camel milk. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammad."
"9995","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar, from al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three I will not abandon: witr before sleep, bathing on Friday, and fasting three days of the month."
"9996","And Muhammad ibn Uthman and Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: With the boy is an aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"9997","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report, he said: The ailment of the believer is expiation for his sins. And we do not know anyone who narrated these hadiths from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Israil."
"9998","Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no contagion and no evil omen. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar."
"9999","Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the story of Dhu al-Yadayn, that he prayed with them, then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Ayyub. And we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of omens except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar, nor the story of Dhu al-Yadayn except Hammad, nor from him except Sulayman ibn Harb."
"10000","And Ibn Ulayyah narrated from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let none of you urinate in stagnant water then perform ablution from it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ibn Ulayyah from Yahya."
"10001","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuzai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands at night, let him open his prayer with two light rakahs."
"10002","Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, Imran ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a dog licks the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"10003","And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: And do all of you find two garments? And Imran ibn Khalid narrated from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, hadiths all of which others of the trustworthy narrated, so we sufficed with what we mentioned of them."
"10004","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Jazari narrated to us, al-Sakan ibn Ismail narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: I have from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two hadiths; one of them that he said: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him. And the other: Whoever marries a woman for a dowry while not intending to fulfill it to her is an adulterer. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin except al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan except al-Sakan, and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Husayn, though it was with others."
"10005","Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Umar ibn Sinan narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, in a raised report: A prophet among the prophets alighted under a tree and an ant stung him, so he ordered that tree to be burned, then Allah revealed to him: Why not a single ant. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Khalid except Umar ibn Sinan."
"10006","9998 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mouse, so he said: A nation from among the nations - or he said - it is said: A nation from among the nations was lost, and I do not know whether it is this one or not; when camel's milk is placed before it, it does not drink it."
"10007","9999 - And Muhammad ibn 'Umarah and Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, they said: Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it. And this hadith is well known from Khalid; more than one narrator reported it from him."
"10008","10000 - 'Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-'Attar narrated to us, Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Name yourselves with my name but do not use my kunyah."
"10009","10001 - And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever points at his brother with a piece of iron, the angels curse him."
"10010","10002 - 'Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Mahbub narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not revile time (al-dahr), for Allah is al-Dahr."
"10011","Jarir ibn Hazim. 10003 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you, with the most tender hearts; faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni."
"10012","10004 - Abu al-Saqr al-Warraq and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Husayn ibn Muhammad informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None of you will be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"10013","10005 - And Abu al-Saqr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Name yourselves with my name, and do not use my kunyah."
"10014","'Imran al-Qattan. 10006 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, Fahd ibn Hayyan narrated to us, 'Imran narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Patience is at the first shock. We do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this channel."
"10015","10007 - Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Sukkari narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, 'Imran, meaning al-Qattan, narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one's deeds will admit him into Paradise nor remove him from the Fire. They said: Not even you? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"10016","Salim Abu Jumay'. 10008 - 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Salim Abu Jumay' narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that 'Umar saw a silk suit being sold and said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you bought this suit and wore it for the delegations that come to you. He said: Silk is worn only by one who has no share in the Hereafter. And we do not know that Salim Abu Jumay' reported from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith; nor do we know anyone else reported it from Ibn Sirin. And others than Salim reported it from Muhammad, from Ibn 'Umar."
"10017","Hisham ibn Hassan. 10009 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When time draws near, the believer's dream will hardly ever lie, and the most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful of them in speech."
"10018","10010 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Placing the hands on the sides (al-ikhtisar) in prayer was forbidden."
"10019","10011 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The five prayers, and Friday to Friday, are expiations for what is between them."
"10020","10012 - And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt; and a woman should not ask for her sister's divorce so as to overturn her bowl and be married instead, for she will have only what Allah has decreed for her."
"10021","10013 - And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into his water for purification until he has poured water over it and washed it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"10022","10014 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best women who ever rode camels are the women of Quraysh: the most affectionate toward a child in his childhood, and the most careful with a husband regarding his property."
"10023","10015 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays, when they came to him, from al-dubba', al-hantam, al-naqir, al-muzaffat, and the leather water-skin with its mouth cut off. And he said: Make nabidh in your water-skin and tie its mouth, and drink what is sweet and wholesome. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me something like this. He said: Then you would make it like - meaning - this, and he described something larger than it."
"10024","10016 - Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On Friday there is an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while asking Allah for good in it except that He grants it to him; he gestured with his hand making it brief."
"10025","10017 - Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah and 'Amr ibn 'Isa narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham - meaning Ibn Hassan - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a town-dweller selling on behalf of a bedouin."
"10026","10018 - Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah and 'Amr ibn 'Isa al-Duba'i narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the incoming caravans (for trade before they reach the market); whoever meets them and buys something from them, its owner has the choice when he reaches the market."
"10027","10019 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good deed is worth ten like it, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it."
"10028","10020 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you forgets while fasting and eats and drinks, then Allah has fed him and given him drink."
"10029","10021 - And with his chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Injury caused by a beast is without liability (jubar), the well is jubar, and in buried treasure (al-rikaz) is the fifth."
"10030","10022 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited, let him accept; if he is fasting, let him invoke blessings (falyusalli)."
"10031","10023 - And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man wore a suit and strutted arrogantly in it, so the earth swallowed him, and he keeps sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"10032","10024 - 'Amr ibn 'Isa narrated to us with his chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is time (al-Dahr)."
"10033","10025 - And with his chain, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"10034","10026 - And with his chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade the earnings of the singing woman and the price of the dog."
"10035","10027 - And with his chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises at night, let him begin his prayer with two light rak'ahs."
"10036","10028 - Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah and 'Amr ibn 'Isa narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you find nothing but camel resting-places and sheepfolds, then pray in the sheepfolds and do not pray in the camel resting-places. And something like this hadith has been reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels, and we do not know it reported with this wording through a sounder chain than this chain with this wording."
"10037","10029 - 'Amr ibn 'Isa narrated to us with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of one of your vessels when a dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first of them with dust."
"10038","10030 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Odd (Witr) and loves the odd."
"10039","10031 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels invoke blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer, as long as he does not break his ablution."
"10040","10032 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in standing water and then bathe from it."
"10041","10033 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied up (musarrah) has the choice for three days; if he returns it, he returns along with it a sa' of wheat, not samra' (a coarser grain)."
"10042","10034 - And with it, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two kinds of wearing: that a man sits wrapping himself in a single garment with nothing of it over his private parts, and that he wraps himself up in a single garment (al-ishtimal)."
"10043","10035 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you lives long will soon meet 'Isa son of Maryam as a rightly-guided Imam and a just arbiter; he will break the cross, kill the pig, and war will lay down its burdens."
"10044","10036 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, and do not use my kunyah."
"10045","10037 - And with it, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot take my likeness."
"10046","10038 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."
"10047","10039 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are like mines; the best of them in the pre-Islamic age are the best of them in Islam, when they gain understanding."
"10048","10040 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its setting place, Allah will turn to him in forgiveness."
"10049","10041 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay the prayer until it cools, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"10050","10042 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for prayer is announced, let none of you hasten to it; let him walk with calmness upon him, then pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"10051","10043 - And with it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angels curse one of you when he points at his brother with a piece of iron, even if he is his full brother through his father and mother."
"10052","10044 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deeds. They said: Not even you? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him."
"10053","10045 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear them both out together (i.e. both sandals), or wear both sandals together."
"10054","10046 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no evil omen, and I love righteous good omens."
"10055","10047 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat she tied up; she neither fed it nor gave it drink, nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth."
"10056","10048 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you outbid his brother, nor propose marriage over his brother's proposal."
"10057","10049 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saying Subhan Allah (tasbih) is for men, and clapping is for women."
"10058","10050 - 'Amr ibn 'Isa and al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in one of the two evening prayers - and my strongest supposition is that it was Zuhr - then he went to a wooden beam at the front of the mosque and placed his hands upon it, one over the other, he said: And among the people were Abu Bakr and 'Umar, who were too awed to speak to him, he said: And the hasty people left and said: The prayer has been shortened, the prayer has been shortened! He said: Then a long-handed man, whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call Dhu al-Yadayn, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: I did not forget, nor has the prayer been shortened. He said: Indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Is Dhu al-Yadayn telling the truth? They said: Yes. So he returned and led us in the remaining two rak'ahs, then gave salutations, then said the takbir while seated, and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said the takbir, then prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said the takbir."
"10059","10051 - Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say 'my slave' or 'my slave-girl'; let him say: my young man and my young woman."
"10060","10052 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali Abu Hafs narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahhab - meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Majid - narrated to us, Hisham - meaning Ibn Hassan - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Sulayman (peace be upon him) said: I shall go around tonight to a hundred women, and every woman among them will give birth to a boy who will strike with the sword in the path of Allah; so he went around to a hundred women, and none of them gave birth except one woman, who gave birth to half a human being. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he made an exception (by saying if Allah wills), every woman among them would have given birth to a boy who would strike with the sword in the path of Allah."
"10061","10053 - And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. And this hadith was reported from Hisham by 'Abd al-Wahhab, Ibn Abi 'Adi, and Rawh - and they raised it (to the Prophet)."
"10062","10054 - And with it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) never lied except for three lies, all of them for the sake of Allah: his saying {Indeed, I am sick}, and his saying {Rather, the eldest of them did it}, and while he was traveling in the land of one of the tyrants, when he stopped at a dwelling, the tyrant was approached and told: A man has stopped here with a woman among the most beautiful of people; so he sent for him and asked him about her, and he said: She is my sister. When he returned to her he said: This one asked me about you, and I said you are my sister, and there is no Muslim today except me and you, and you are my sister, so do not belie me in his presence. She was taken to him, and when he reached out to take her he was seized, so he said: Supplicate Allah for me and I will not harm you. So she supplicated for him and he was released; then he reached out to take her and was seized likewise or more severely, and said: Supplicate Allah for me and I will not harm you. So she supplicated and he was released, three times. Then he summoned the nearest of his attendants and said: You have not brought me a human being, but you have brought me a devil; take her out and give her Hajar. She came back while Ibrahim was standing in prayer, and when he sensed her he turned and said: What happened? She said: Allah sufficed against the scheming of the wrongdoer, and he gave her Hajar as a servant. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith with a connected chain from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hisham, and others reported it as stopped (mawquf)."
"10063","10055 - And with it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Adam and Musa disputed; Musa said to him: Are you Adam who brought misery upon people and expelled them from Paradise? Adam said to him: Are you Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, and upon whom He sent down the Torah? He said: Yes. Then did you find that He had decreed that upon me before He created me? He said: Yes. So Adam overcame Musa (peace be upon them both)."
"10064","10056 - And with it, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: People disputed in his presence - or discussed in his presence - so he said: What are you discussing? They said: Are men more numerous or women? Abu Hurayrah said: The first group to enter Paradise, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon, and those who follow them like the brightest brilliant star in the sky; each man among them will have two wives, the marrow of whose shins will be seen from behind the flesh; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no unmarried person in it. And I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10065","10057 - 'Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan al-'Uqayli narrated to us, Hisham - meaning Ibn Hassan - narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it in, for in one of its wings is a disease and in the other is a cure."
"10066","10058 - 'Amr ibn 'Isa and Jamil ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman does not marry off a woman, nor does a woman marry herself off; for the adulteress is the one who marries herself off. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel from Abu Hurayrah, nor do we know anyone who reported it with a connected chain from Hisham except Muhammad ibn Marwan and 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb."
"10067","10059 - Jamil ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Milk in a dream is the natural disposition (fitrah). And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith from Hisham except Muhammad ibn Marwan and 'Awn ibn 'Umarah, and 'Awn is lenient in hadith."
"10068","10060 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hospitality is three days; whatever exceeds that is charity."
"10069","10061 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Salih ibn Bishr al-Murri narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Call upon Allah while you are certain of an answer, and know that Allah does not accept supplication from a heedless, inattentive heart. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by Abu Hurayrah with this chain, nor do we know anyone who reported it from Hisham except Salih al-Murri, and he was one of the worshippers whose worship, in our view, occupied him from memorizing hadith."
"10070","10062 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Mihja' narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to know what standing he has with Allah, let him know what standing Allah has with him. And we do not know this hadith reported except by Abu Hurayrah with this chain, nor did anyone report it from Hisham except Salih."
"10071","10063 - 'Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while we were disputing about predestination, and he became angry until his face reddened, until it was as though pomegranate seeds had been burst open on his cheeks; then he turned to us and said: Is it with this that you were commanded? Is it with this that I was sent to you? Those before you perished only when they disputed about this matter; I adjure you not to dispute about it. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurayrah with this wording except with this chain, nor do we know anyone who reported it except Salih."
"10072","10064 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: I sowed (zara'tu); let him say: I plowed (harathtu)."
"10073","10065 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that an immoral woman saw a dog on a hot day circling a well, its tongue hanging out from thirst, so she took off her leather sock for it and gave it water, and she was forgiven."
"10074","10066 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Men will be carried so far by questioning that they will say: Allah created creation, so who created Him?"
"10075","10067 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I saw myself falling down between the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the chamber of 'A'ishah, overcome from hunger, and I would be carried, and I would say: It is not that; it is only hunger."
"10076","10068 - Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Muqaddam al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya ibn 'Ata' ibn Muqaddam narrated to me, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Earth (to strike for tayammum) is the ablution of the Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years; when he finds water, let him fear Allah and touch his skin with it, for that is better. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this channel, and we heard it only from Muqaddam ibn Muhammad from his uncle; and Muqaddam was trustworthy, of well-known lineage."
"10077","10069 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulathah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Peoples who raise their eyes to the sky in prayer will surely stop, or their sight will surely be snatched away. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this channel with this chain."
"10078","10070 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I love beauty, and I have been given of it such that I do not like anyone among people to surpass me - either he said: by a sandal strap, or: by a sandal thong - is that part of arrogance? He said: No; but arrogance is rejecting the truth and despising people. And we heard this hadith only from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi', from 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Hisham."
"10079","10071 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays Abu Mu'awiyah al-Za'farani narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The sandals of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two straps (qibalan). And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this channel, nor did anyone report it from Hisham except 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays, and there is leniency in his hadith."
"10080","10072 - Muhammad ibn Thawab narrated to us, Husayn - meaning Ibn 'Ali - narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we attain our women in Paradise? He said: Yes, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul; a man will indeed attain a hundred virgins in a single day. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, except Husayn ibn 'Ali."
"10081","10073 - Al-'Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to his family and saw the need they were in, so he went out to the desert. His wife said: O Allah, grant us something to grind, or something to knead and bake. Then the bowl was full of bread, the millstone was grinding, and the oven was full of sides of roast meat. Her husband came and said: Do you have anything? She said: The provision of Allah - or: Allah has provided. He lifted the millstone and swept what was around it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he left it, it would have ground until the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith from Hisham except Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash."
"10082","10074 - Al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim al-'Anbari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man lie skin-to-skin with a man, nor a woman with a woman. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this channel, and none reported it from Hisham except Abu Bakr."
"10083","10075 - Al-'Abbas ibn 'Abdullah al-Tarfa'i narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade plundering (al-nuhbah). And others than Abu Bakr reported this hadith from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas."
"10084","10076 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: the rich are invited and the poor are kept out; and whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"10085","10077 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us with his chain, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a man supplicating and pointing with two fingers, so he grasped one of them, or said: One, one. And we do not know anyone who reported these hadiths from Hisham ibn Hassan except Makhlad ibn Husayn."
"10086","10078 - And with it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade selling food until two measures pass into it, so that the increase is for its owner and the loss upon him."
"10087","10079 - 'Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Discussion of predestination has been deferred for the worst of people at the end of time. And we do not know for this hadith any channel from Abu Hurayrah other than this channel ... sound, nor do we know anyone who reported it from Hisham except 'Umar ibn Abi Khalifah."
"10088","10080 - The hadith of Dawud ibn Bakr al-Tustari, who said: Hibban ibn Aghlab narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise."
"10089","10081 - And Dawud ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hibban ibn Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The treasuries of Allah are speech (al-kalam); when He intends a thing, He says to it: Be - and it is. And we do not know anyone who reported these two hadiths from Hisham except Aghlab, nor do we know anyone who reported them from Aghlab except his son; and al-Aghlab was not strong, though more than one of the early scholars narrated from him."
"10090","10082 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya Abu 'Ali al-Darir narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into food and drink."
"10091","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Musnad of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) [Sequel: Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id] 1/1 - ... and give zakah, fast Ramadan, give a fifth of the spoils, and I forbid you four things: al-dubba', al-hantam, al-muzaffat, and al-naqir. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is your knowledge of al-naqir? He said: A trunk which they hollow out and warm dates and water in it, until when its boiling subsides you drink it, until one of you strikes his cousin with the sword - and among the people was a man who had suffered such a wound; so he kept hiding it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - They said: O Messenger of Allah, then in what shall we drink? He said: In leather water-skins whose mouths are tied shut. They said: O Messenger of Allah, our land has many rats and leather water-skins do not last for us. He said: Even if the rats eat them, even if the rats eat them - twice, or three times. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj 'Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits which Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, loves: forbearance and deliberateness. And we do not know this hadith in its entirety reported from Abu Sa'id except through this channel with this chain. 2/2 And 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la reported it from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - with the like of it. Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated it to us, he said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us."
"10092","3/3 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id: That the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in al-hantam, al-muzaffat, and al-dubba', and mixing unripe dates with ripe dates, and raisins with dates."
"10093","4/4 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after 'Asr until the sun sets. And he forbade fasting two days: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice. And we do not know this hadith reported from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, except by Hammad ibn Salamah."
"10094","5/5 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10095","6/6 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hospitality is three days; whatever is besides that is charity. And we do not know this hadith reported from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, except by Hammad ibn Salamah."
"10096","7/7 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar - Bundar - narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to recite in our prayer the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah) and whatever is easy. And we do not know this hadith reported from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, except by Hammam."
"10097","8/8 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform witr before you enter morning. And I think Hibban erred in this hadith, for it is only known from the hadith of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id; Hammam and others reported it."
"10098","9/9 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Kabir al-'Attar narrated to us, they said: 'Amr ibn 'Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-'Awwam - meaning 'Imran al-Qattan - narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man from my ummah will rule - or he said: from me, I think he said - with a high-bridged nose and a broad forehead; he will fill the earth with justice and equity as it was filled with tyranny and wrongdoing; he will live like this - and he spread his left hand and two fingers of his right hand, the index finger and the thumb, and clenched three. And we do not know this hadith reported from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, except by 'Imran al-Qattan. 'Amr ibn 'Asim al-Kilabi: there is no harm in him."
"10099","10/10 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id - I think he raised it - who said: My ummah will be two factions; a renegade group (mariqah) will emerge between them, and the one of them closer to the truth will undertake killing them. And we do not know this hadith reported from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, except by Abu 'Awanah."
"10100","11/11 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We were sitting at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), discussing; this one cited a verse and this one a verse. He said: Then he said: [...] What are these? Is it for this that you were sent? Or with this were you commanded? Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks. [source has an ellipsis of dots indicating a lacuna]."
"10101","12/12 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Suwayd narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas - with the like of it. And we do not know this hadith reported except by Suwayd Abu Hatim, the food merchant; he is Suwayd ibn Ibrahim, from whom Safwan ibn 'Isa and a group reported; there is no harm in him. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak is a trustworthy Basran."
"10102","13/13 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id: {And whoever turns his back to them on that day} - he said: It was revealed on the day of Badr."
"10103","14/14 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: It was revealed on the day of Badr: {And whoever turns his back to them on that day}."
"10104","15/15 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from ... [truncated in source; the chain ends incomplete]."
"10105","16/16 - [Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, Asid ibn Zayd narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Awf, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, then with it - and excellent is it], and whoever bathes, then bathing is better. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel. Nor do we know anyone who reported it from 'Awf except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Asid ibn Zayd. And Asid ibn Zayd is a Kufan; his hadith has been tolerated despite a severe Shi'ism that was in him."
"10106","17/17 - Ibrahim ibn Hani' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahib narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from 'Awf, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the two prayers while traveling. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Sa'id except through this channel, nor did anyone report it from 'Awf except Abu Shihab. And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahib is a well-known, trustworthy Baghdadi man [...] he was one of the worshippers. [source has an ellipsis of dots]."
"10107","18/18 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu Qaza'ah informed me, he said: Abu Nadrah and Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what drink is lawful for us? He said: Do not drink in al-naqir. They said: What is al-naqir? He said: The palm trunk hollowed out, in which nabidh is made. Nor in al-dubba', nor al-hantam [...] And upon you is al-muka - upon you is al-muka. [source has an ellipsis of dots indicating a lacuna]. And we do not know that Abu Qaza'ah reported from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, except this hadith. And Abu Qaza'ah is a Basran, there is no harm in him; Shu'bah, Hammad ibn Salamah, and Muhammad ibn Juhadah reported from him. Abu Bakr said: 'And Hasan' means al-Hasan al-Basri. And al-Hasan reported two or three hadiths from Abu Sa'id but did not hear from him."
"10108","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla of the people of Kufah. 19/19 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban - meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with truffles (akmu') in his hand and said: These are from the manna, and they are a cure for the eye. And there has been disagreement about this hadith from al-A'mash, and we do not know anyone who said: from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Sa'id, except Shayban and Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym. Nor do we know that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla reported with a connected chain from Abu Sa'id except this hadith. And 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla is among the eminent Followers; he reported from a large group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they are a household all of whom narrated: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla and his father reported hadiths from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and the sons of 'Abd al-Rahman: 'Isa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman. As for 'Isa, he heard from his father and narrated from him; as for Muhammad, he did not hear from his father but narrated from his brother 'Isa from his father, and from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah from his father; and Muhammad was one of the jurists of Kufah, but weak in memory in hadith. And the son of Muhammad narrated, namely 'Imran ibn Muhammad; he reported from his father, and we do not know that he reported from anyone other than his father. And the son of 'Imran, Muhammad ibn 'Imran ibn Muhammad, narrated from his father from his grandfather, and from others than his father; and he had compiled the laws of inheritance. As for 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman: he heard from his grandfather 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, and he is older than his uncle Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman."
"10109","Al-Agharr Abu Muslim. 20/20 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban - meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes at night and wakes his wife, and they pray two rak'ahs together, they are recorded among the men who remember Allah much and the women who remember. And we do not know this hadith reported except by Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain."
"10110","21/21 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim - and he is a Kufan - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man reciting Surat al-Kahf, and when he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he fell silent. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the assembly with whom I was commanded to keep myself patient. Abu Bakr said: Thus Abu Ahmad reported it, from 'Amr ibn Thabit, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr - as mursal."
"10111","22/22 - And Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by while a man was reciting Surat al-Hijr - or Surat al-Kahf - and he fell silent, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the assembly with whom I was commanded to [...] keep myself patient. [source has an ellipsis of dots]. And Muhammad ibn al-Salt connected this hadith, and we do not know anyone who connected it other than him. Nor do we know that 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar reported with a connected chain from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, except these two hadiths."
"10112","23/23 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, who said: I bear witness regarding Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, that they both bore witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No people sit remembering Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, and Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, mentions them among those with Him. And this hadith has been reported from Abu Hurayrah through other channels; and we do not know it reported from Abu Sa'id except through this [...] [truncated in source]."
"10113","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Musnad of 'A'ishah, Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her) ['Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from her] In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah. Abu 'Umar Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: 24/1 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, from a single vessel."
"10114","25/2 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel; and he would begin by washing what had touched him, then perform his ablution for prayer, then run his fingers through his head twice, then pour over his head three times, then pour the remainder of his water over his body."
"10115","26/3 - And Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - with the like of it. And Ayyub and 'Ubaydullah reported this hadith, and we do not know anyone who reported it from 'Ubaydullah except al-Mu'tamir. And we heard it only from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Ayyub. And it is well known from 'A'ishah."
"10116","27/4 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah: That Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer from prolonged bleeding and do not become pure; shall I abandon prayer? He said: That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation comes, leave prayer; and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray. I said to Hisham: A single washing? He said: Yes. And this hadith has been reported from 'A'ishah through various channels with differing wordings, each wording entailing a ruling of its own; for that reason we made them separate hadiths due to the difference in their wordings."
"10117","28/5 - 'Amr narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lighten the two rak'ahs of dawn. And we do not know this hadith reported with this wording except by 'A'ishah."
"10118","29/6 - 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah: That a boy was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he urinated in his lap, so he followed it with water. And we do not know this hadith reported from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) except from the hadith of Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah."
"10119","30/7 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah: {And neither recite aloud in your prayer nor lower it} - he said: It was revealed concerning supplication. And al-Thawri also reported this hadith from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah."
"10120","31/8 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrating from his father, from 'A'ishah, that she said: A garment from the garments of Syria was gifted to us, called Dhawat al-Khayl (those with horses), and I took it as a curtain, she said: When he came and saw it, he tore it down - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) [...] [truncated in source]."
"10121","32/9 - [... Eat unripe dates with ripe dates], for Satan grieves when he sees the son of Adam eating it, saying: The son of Adam has lived until he ate the old with the new. [the beginning of the chain is missing in source]. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays."
"10122","33/10 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to me, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard sounds and said: What are these sounds? They said: The palm trees - they are pollinating them. He said: Had they not done it, it would have been fine. So they refrained from it, and it became shis (poor-quality dates). They mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: If it is something of your worldly affairs, then it is your concern; and if it is something of your religious affairs, then it is for me. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Hammad ibn Salamah; and others than Hammad reported it from Hisham, from his father, as mursal."
"10123","34/11 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fever is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool it with water."
"10124","35/12 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah: That Hind bint 'Utbah said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Sufyan is a miserly man; he does not give me and my child what suffices us, except that I take from him without his knowledge. He said: Take what suffices you and your child, according to what is customary."
"10125","36/13 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ruqyah, saying: O Allah, remove the affliction, Lord of mankind; none removes evil except You."
"10126","37/14 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When prayer is established and supper is brought near, then eat, then pray."
"10127","38/15 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah. [the matn is missing in source]."
"10128","39/16 - And Muhammad ibn 'Umarah narrated it to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When supper is placed and prayer is established, begin with supper."
"10129","40/17 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel; he would begin by washing what had touched him, then perform his ablution for prayer, then run his fingers through his head twice, then pour over his head three times, then pour the remainder of his water over his body."
"10130","41/18 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Amir ibn Ibrahim al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: 'Anbasah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death by confinement (qatl al-sabr) - no sin passes it except that it effaces it. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who reported the hadith of Hisham with a connected chain except Ya'qub from 'Anbasah."
"10131","42/19 - Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: 'Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah - she raised the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I hesitate to raise it - he said: Do not seek milk from a foolish woman, for milk transmits traits. And we do not preserve this hadith raised except through this channel, and 'Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim is lenient in hadith, though his hadith has been tolerated."
"10132","43/20 - 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: Bilal came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during his illness and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; when he stands in your place he weeps. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She repeated to him, and he said: You are like the companions of Yusuf."
"10133","44/21 - 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: When you enter ihram, say: My place of release is where You restrain me. And we do not know anyone who reported this with a connected chain from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Abu Usamah; others than Abu Usamah reported it as mursal. And some people said: from Duba'ah."
"10134","45/22 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said during his illness: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. So I said to Hafsah: Say: Abu Bakr, when he stands, will not make the people hear from weeping; so Hafsah said it to him. He said: You are the companions of Yusuf; command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer."
"10135","46/23 - 'Umar ibn Musa al-Jari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me, they fattened me but I did not gain weight, until they fattened me with cucumbers and fresh dates, and I gained weight upon it in the finest manner."
"10136","47/24 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah - with the like of it. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"10137","48/25 - Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn 'Imran al-Ja'fari narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry suitable equals (al-akfa'). And we do not know anyone who reported it with a connected chain except al-Harith ibn 'Imran, and he was not followed in it."
"10138","49/26 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: Khawlah bint Hakim came to me - and she was under 'Uthman ibn Maz'un - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the shabbiness of her appearance and said: O 'A'ishah, how shabby is the appearance of Khawlah! She said: She is a woman with no husband; he fasts the day and stands at night, so she is like one with no husband, and she has neglected herself and wasted it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for 'Uthman ibn Maz'un and said: Is it aversion to my way? He said: No, by Allah, but your way is what I seek. He said: I sleep and pray, fast and break fast, and marry women; so fear Allah, O 'Uthman, for your family has a right upon you, your eye has a right upon you, and your soul has a right upon you; so fast and break fast, pray and sleep. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Ibn Ishaq, nor do we know it reported from 'A'ishah through any other channel."
"10139","50/27 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid and al-'Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he heard the muezzin say - ... - would say: And I, and I. [source has an ellipsis]. And more than one reported this hadith from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, as mursal; and 'Ali ibn Mushir and Hafs ibn Ghiyath reported it with a connected chain from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah. And 'Amr ibn Maymun reported it from his father, from 'A'ishah."
"10140","51/28 - 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who came to me while I was at al-'Aqiq said: You are in a [...] blessed valley. [source has an ellipsis of dots]. And we do not know anyone who reported it with a connected chain from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Abu Usamah; others reported it as mursal."
"10141","52/29 - Yahya ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It harms no woman to settle between two houses of the Ansar, or to settle with her parents. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Hisham ibn 'Urwah except Hisham ibn Hassan, nor from Hisham ibn Hassan except Rawh ibn 'Ubadah; and we do not know anyone who narrated it among those whose hadith is not rejected except Ahmad and Yahya ibn Habib. And a group other than them reported it and lied in it."
"10142","53/30 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment is vinegar. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"10143","54/31 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No house with dates in it is without provision. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"10144","55/32 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, they said: 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give a single salutation. And more than one reported this hadith as stopped (mawquf), and we do not know anyone who reported it with a connected chain except 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah from Zuhayr."
"10145","56/33 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us - and the wording is Ibn Miskin's - they said: 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah Abu Hafs al-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is no burden upon one of you to take two garments for his Friday besides his work clothes. And we do not know this hadith reported from 'A'ishah except through this channel with this chain, nor do we know anyone who narrated it except 'Amr from Zuhayr."
"10146","57/34 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to me, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of a woman is like a rib; if you straighten it you break it, and if you enjoy it you enjoy it while there is crookedness in it. And we do not know anyone who reported it with a connected chain from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Zuhayr and Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash."
"10147","58/35 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the child belongs to the bed. And Hisham only reports this hadith from his father as mursal; and al-Zuhri reported it with a connected chain from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah. And we do not know anyone who reported it with a connected chain from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"10148","59/36 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, except Zam'ah."
"10149","60/37 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: People used to pour forth - and he mentioned a word - so it was revealed: {Then pour forth from where the people pour forth}."
"10150","61/38 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray five rak'ahs at night."
"10151","62 / 39 - Abduh ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: Aflah ibn Abi al-Qu'ays came seeking permission to enter upon me, and I refused to permit him. He said: I am your uncle. I said: It was only the woman who suckled me, and the man did not suckle me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, so I told him, and he said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you."
"10152","63 / 40 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three Sahuli cotton garments, among them neither a shirt nor a turban."
"10153","64 / 41 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: Safiyyah was from the safi (select portion of spoils)."
"10154","65 / 42 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while he was fasting."
"10155","66 / 43 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs in the night."
"10156","67 / 44 - Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah."
"10157","68 / 45 - And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When supper is served and the prayer is established, begin with supper."
"10158","69 / 46 - Muhammad ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform his ablution for prayer - meaning: in the ghusl of janabah."
"10159","70 / 47 - Muhammad ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: He only camped at al-Abtah - meaning: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - so that it would be easier for his departure."
"10160","71 / 48 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer istihadah; shall I leave the prayer? He said: That is only a vein; when menstruation comes, leave the prayer, and when it goes, wash and pray."
"10161","72 / 49 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Manzur narrated to us, he said: Attaf narrated to me from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No caution avails against decree, and supplication avails - I think he said - against what has not yet descended, and supplication meets affliction and they contend together until the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this isnad."
"10162","73 / 50 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: concerning His saying: {And do not recite loudly in your prayer nor be silent in it}: she said: It was revealed concerning supplication."
"10163","74 / 51 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness was never in a people except that it benefited them, nor harshness in a people except that it harmed them."
"10164","75 / 52 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: I said: How is it that each of your wives has a kunyah? So give me a kunyah - I think he said - so he gave me the kunyah Umm Abdullah."
"10165","76 / 53 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Wazir Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: al-Darawardi narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that a people raided the milch camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with an isnad from Aishah except al-Darawardi. And others narrated it from Hisham, from his father, mursal."
"10166","77 / 54 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor does he steal while he is a believer when he steals."
"10167","78 / 55 - And Ahmad ibn Aban narrated it to us from al-Darawardi, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah - mawquf."
"10168","79 / 56 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah narrated to us, he said: Hafs narrated to us - I think him: Ibn Abdullah - from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not explain anything of the Qur'an except verses in number which Jibril taught him."
"10169","80 / 57 - Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah."
"10170","81 / 58 - And from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad al-Hajj)."
"10171","82 / 59 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to clean his teeth with the siwak while two men were with him, one older than his companion, so Allah revealed to him concerning the merit of the siwak to give it to the elder. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid."
"10172","83 / 60 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: When the polytheists were routed on the day of Uhud with a rout recognized among them, a caller cried out: Where are the servants of Allah? She said: So their front returned and they fought, they and their rear. Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman looked, and there was his father, so he said: My father, my father. She said: By Allah, they did not hold back until they killed him. So Hudhayfah said: May Allah forgive you. Urwah said: There remained in Hudhayfah something of it until he met Allah."
"10173","84 / 61 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Qurran al-Asadi narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, every Prophet has a hawari (disciple), and my hawari is al-Zubayr."
"10174","85 / 62 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: Salma, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - wife of Abu Rafi' - came and said: He beats her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Rafi': What is the matter with you and her? He said: She harms me, O Messenger of Allah. She said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not harm him with anything, but he broke wind while praying, so I said to him: O Abu Rafi', the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the Muslims that when wind comes out of one of them he should perform ablution, so he got up beating me. She said: So the Messenger of Allah began laughing and saying: O Abu Rafi', she commanded you only with good. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah except Ibn Ishaq."
"10175","86 / 63 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Nafi' narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two prostrations of forgetfulness are for every addition or decrease. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this isnad."
"10176","87 / 64 - al-Nadr ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set up a pulpit for Hassan ibn Thabit to satirize the polytheists upon it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah with this wording except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"10177","88 / 65 - Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Umayr narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a slaughter camel from a Bedouin for a wasq of Ajwah dates, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought dates but did not find them, so the Bedouin objected and shouted: O treachery! So the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O enemy of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for the one with a right has speech. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Khawlah bint Hakim, saying: Tell her: I bought from this Bedouin a slaughter camel for a wasq of Ajwah dates but did not find it with my family, so lend me a wasq of Ajwah for this Bedouin. So she answered him, and when the Bedouin took possession he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to him: Have you taken possession? He said: Yes, you have fulfilled and done well. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are those who fulfill and do well. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah except Yahya ibn Umayr."
"10178","89 / 66 - Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Isma'il ibn Ayyub ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ate food, his hand did not go beyond what was before him, but when dates were brought his hand roamed. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah, from the Prophet, except from this angle with this isnad."
"10179","90 / 67 - Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant says: O Lord, O Lord, four times, Allah, blessed and exalted, says: At your service, My servant; ask, you shall be given. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah except from this angle, nor do we know it narrated from other than Aishah with this wording."
"10180","91 / 68 - Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dead person dies, leave him alone. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah except from this angle with this isnad. And Abdullah ibn Uthman is a well-known man from the people of Basrah."
"10181","92 / 69 - Ishaq ibn Sulayman Abu Ya'qub al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a woman shaving her head. And we do not know anyone who corroborated Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman in his narration, and he narrated from Abd al-Hamid hadiths in which he was not corroborated."
"10182","Follow-up: Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah, from Urwah. 93 / 70 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah narrated to me from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, Zaynab his daughter left Makkah with Kinanah - or: Ibn Kinanah - so they went out after her, and Habbar ibn al-Aswad caught up with her and kept thrusting at her camel with his spear until he threw her down and she cast what was in her womb, and she bled profusely, and she carried (a child). Then Banu Hashim and Banu Umayyah disputed over her; Banu Umayyah said: We have more right to her, and she was under their cousin Abu al-As, and she was with Hind bint Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, and Hind used to say to her: This is because of your father. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd ibn Harithah: Will you not go and bring Zaynab? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take my ring and give it to her. So Zayd went and kept being gentle until he met a shepherd and said: For whom do you herd? He said: For Abu al-As. He said: Whose are these sheep? He said: Zaynab bint Muhammad's. So he walked with him a little, then said: Will you take something to give her without mentioning it to anyone? He said: Yes - so he gave him the ring. The shepherd went and brought in his sheep and gave her the ring, and she recognized it. She said: Who gave you this? He said: A man. She said: And where did you leave him? He said: In such-and-such place. So she waited until night came, then she went out to him, and when she came to him Zayd said to her: Ride in front of him on his camel. She said: No, but you ride in front of me. So he rode and she rode behind him until she arrived. The Messenger of Allah used to say: She is the best of my daughters; she was afflicted for my sake. That reached Ali ibn Husayn, so he went to Urwah and said: What is a hadith that reached me from you in which you narrate diminishing the right of Fatimah? Urwah said: By Allah, I would not love to have what is between the east and the west if I diminished Fatimah of a right belonging to her; as for after this, I shall never narrate it again. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Urwah with this wording except Umar ibn Abdullah."
"10183","94 / 71 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, he said: Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah narrated to me that he heard Urwah and al-Qasim reporting from Aishah that she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands with dharirah in the Farewell Pilgrimage for exiting ihram and for entering ihram, and when he entered ihram, and when he stoned the Aqabah on the day of sacrifice before circumambulating the House."
"10184","What the shaykhs narrated from Urwah. 95 / 72 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from a man - I think him from the family of al-Mu'alla - from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Aishah informed him that she heard the Messenger of Allah saying: Buthan is upon a blessing ............... from the blessings of Paradise."
"10185","96 / 73 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn al-Khalil narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Musafi' ibn Abdullah, from Urwah, from Aishah: that a woman said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should a woman wash when she has a wet dream and sees water? So Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said to her: May your hands be dusty. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Leave her; is resemblance from other than that? If her water overcomes the man's water, the child resembles his maternal uncles, and if the man's water overcomes her water, he resembles him."
"10186","97 / 74 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr who said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No calamity befalls the believer, even a thorn, except that sins are requited thereby - or expiated thereby - from his sins. He does not know which of the two Urwah said."
"10187","Abd al-Wahid ibn Maymun from Urwah. Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: 98 / 75 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Maymun narrated to us - and he is a man from the people of Madinah, kunyah Abu Hamzah - from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him wash."
"10188","99 / 76 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Maymun narrated to us from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Whoever humiliates a wali of Mine has made war upon Me lawful, and My servant does not draw near to Me with anything like performing My obligations, and My servant keeps drawing near to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him; when I love him I become his eye with which he sees, his ear with which he hears, his hand with which he strikes, his heart with which he understands, and his tongue with which he speaks. If he calls upon Me I answer him, if he asks Me I give him, and I have never hesitated over anything I do as I hesitate over his death, for he hates death and I hate displeasing him."
"10189","100 / 77 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Maymun narrated to us from Urwah, from Aishah who said: Whoever leaves Friday prayer three times, his heart is sealed. And I saw it in my book from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I feared to raise it (as marfu'). And we do not know that Abd al-Wahid ibn Maymun narrated with an isnad from Urwah except these hadiths, nor do we know anyone who shared them with him from Urwah nor from Aishah."
"10190","Yazid ibn Ruman from Urwah. 101 / 78 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning the slain that they be dragged to the well, they were thrown into it - except what was of Umayyah ibn Khalaf, for he disintegrated - or swelled - in his armor and filled it, so they went to take him out and he fell apart, so they left him and cast earth and stones upon him - then when they were cast into the well, the Messenger of Allah stood over them and said: O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to dead people?! He said: They have known that what I promised them is true. Aishah said: While people say: They heard what you said, but it is only: They have known."
"10191","102 / 79 - And Umar ibn Shabbah narrated it to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: I read to Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - the like of it. al-Bazzar said: We do not know anyone who narrated it in full except Yazid ibn Ruman, and part of it was narrated from more than one angle."
"10192","Follow-up: al-Zuhri, from Urwah. 103 / 80 ... The angel of the mountains was sent to you, so the angel of the mountains called me and greeted me and said: O Muhammad, Allah has heard the saying of your people and what they returned to you, and He has sent me to you so that you command me with what you wish; if you wish I shall close the two Akhshabs over them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather I hope that Allah will bring forth from their loins those who worship Allah alone, associating nothing with Him. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10193","104 / 81 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah said: Allah, blessed and exalted, does not take knowledge away from people by snatching after He has given it to them, but He takes away the scholars; every time a scholar goes, what he had of knowledge goes with him, until there remain those who do not know, so they go astray and lead astray. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah except Yunus. And Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"10194","105 / 82 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No calamity befalls the Muslim except that Allah expiates thereby, even a thorn that pricks him. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Aishah."
"10195","106 / 83 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake in the morning junub, then dawn would overtake him while he was junub in Ramadan without a wet dream, then he would wash and fast. And this hadith is only known from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah and Umm Salamah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Urwah and Abu Bakr except Yunus. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10196","107 / 84 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: A man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and sat before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have slaves who betray me, lie to me and disobey me, so I revile them and beat them; where do I stand concerning them? He said: Your punishment and their sins are weighed; if your punishment is less than their sins, the merit is yours, and if your punishment equals their sins, there is neither for you nor against you, and if your punishment is severer than their sins, retribution will be taken from you for them on the Day of Resurrection. So the man began crying out and weeping before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What is the matter with you? Do you not read the Book of Allah: {And We shall set up the just balances for the Day of Resurrection}, the verse. So the man said: O Messenger of Allah, they are free. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Layth except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan, from al-Layth, from Malik. And he was not corroborated."
"10197","108 / 85 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The merit of prayer with siwak over prayer without siwak is seventyfold. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording except Ibn Ishaq, nor did anyone narrate it from Ibn Ishaq except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd. And Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated something close to it."
"10198","109 / 86 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Yahya narrated to us with it, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two rak'ahs with siwak are better than seventy rak'ahs without siwak. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10199","110 / 87 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to test women in the pledge, reciting to them this verse: {When the believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery}; by Allah, his hand never touched the hand of a woman in a pledge at all. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10200","111 / 88 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of Asr before the sun sets, or a rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises, has caught it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
